WEBVTT

01:13.413 --> 01:15.413
l can't let you out, Hedwig.

01:15.583 --> 01:19.133
l'm not allowed to use magic
outside of school.

01:19.593 --> 01:23.463
-Besides, if Uncle Vernon--
-Harry Potter!

01:25.303 --> 01:26.933
Now you've done it.

01:31.763 --> 01:34.433
He's in there. Vernon?

01:36.773 --> 01:40.563
l'm warning you, if you can't control
that bloody bird, it'll have to go.

01:41.113 --> 01:42.523
But she's bored.

01:42.693 --> 01:47.203
lf l could only let her out
for an hour or two.

01:47.363 --> 01:51.333
So you can send secret messages
to your freaky little friends? No, sir.

01:51.493 --> 01:56.623
But l haven't had any messages
from any of my friends.

01:56.793 --> 01:58.463
Not one. . .

01:58.873 --> 02:00.333
. . .all summer.

02:00.503 --> 02:03.753
Who would want to be
friends with you?

02:06.013 --> 02:08.473
l should think you'd be
a little more grateful.

02:08.633 --> 02:12.143
We've raised you since you were a baby,
given you the food off our table. . .

02:12.303 --> 02:14.433
. . .even let you have
Dudley's second bedroom. . .

02:14.603 --> 02:17.143
. . .purely out of the goodness
of our hearts.

02:17.563 --> 02:19.813
Not now.
lt's for when the Masons arrive.

02:20.273 --> 02:23.323
Which should be any minute.

02:23.983 --> 02:26.823
Now, let's go over our schedule
once again, shall we?

02:26.993 --> 02:28.903
Petunia, when the Masons arrive,
you will be. . .?

02:29.073 --> 02:32.783
ln the lounge, waiting to welcome
them graciously to our home.

02:32.953 --> 02:36.873
-Good. And, Dudley, you will be. . .?
-l'll be waiting to open the door.

02:37.043 --> 02:38.963
Excellent.

02:43.503 --> 02:45.343
And you?

02:45.923 --> 02:50.303
l'll be in my bedroom, making no noise
and pretending that l don't exist.

02:50.473 --> 02:52.183
Too right, you will.

02:52.343 --> 02:55.853
With any luck, this could be the day
l make the biggest deal of my career. . .

02:56.023 --> 02:59.563
. . .and you will not mess it up.

03:10.703 --> 03:15.533
Harry Potter, such an honor it is.

03:18.413 --> 03:23.333
-Who are you?
-Dobby, sir. Dobby the house-elf.

03:24.083 --> 03:25.423
Not to be rude or anything. . .

03:25.593 --> 03:29.553
. . .but this isn't a great time for me
to have a house-elf in my bedroom.

03:29.723 --> 03:32.223
Yes, sir. Dobby understands.

03:32.383 --> 03:35.513
lt's just that Dobby
has come to tell you. . . .

03:35.683 --> 03:40.523
lt is difficult, sir.
Dobby wonders where to begin.

03:40.683 --> 03:46.483
-Why don't you sit down?
-Sit down? Sit down?

03:49.743 --> 03:54.243
Dobby, l'm sorry. l didn't mean
to offend you or anything.

03:54.413 --> 03:56.583
Offend Dobby?

03:56.743 --> 03:59.083
Dobby has heard
of your greatness, sir. . .

03:59.243 --> 04:05.043
. . .but never has he been asked
to sit down by a wizard, like an equal.

04:05.963 --> 04:08.593
You can't have met
many decent wizards then.

04:08.753 --> 04:11.173
No, l haven't.

04:11.343 --> 04:14.093
That was an awful thing to say.

04:14.763 --> 04:18.223
-Bad Dobby! Bad Dobby!
-Stop, Dobby. Dobby, shush.

04:18.393 --> 04:19.773
Dobby, please, stop.

04:24.273 --> 04:26.903
Don't mind that. lt's just the cat.

04:28.823 --> 04:33.363
-Bad Dobby.
-Stop! Stop, Dobby. Please, be quiet.

04:33.533 --> 04:35.823
Are you all right?

04:36.573 --> 04:39.453
Dobby had to punish himself, sir.

04:39.623 --> 04:42.833
Dobby almost spoke ill
of his family, sir.

04:43.003 --> 04:46.963
-Your family?
-The wizard family Dobby serves, sir.

04:47.133 --> 04:50.133
Dobby is bound to serve
one family forever.

04:50.303 --> 04:52.843
lf they ever knew Dobby was here. . . .

04:54.473 --> 05:00.263
But Dobby had to come. Dobby has
to protect Harry Potter. To warn him.

05:00.433 --> 05:02.733
Harry Potter must not go back. . .

05:02.893 --> 05:07.603
. . .to Hogwarts School
of Witchcraft and Wizardry this year.

05:07.773 --> 05:12.943
There is a plot, a plot to make
most terrible things happen.

05:13.113 --> 05:16.453
What terrible things?
Who's plotting them?

05:17.323 --> 05:19.783
Can't say.

05:20.243 --> 05:25.963
-Okay, l understand. You can't say.
-Don't make me talk. l--

05:27.373 --> 05:30.673
-Dobby. Dobby, put the lamp down.
-Bad Dobby.

05:30.843 --> 05:34.883
So when they arrive
at the ninth hole. . . .

05:37.473 --> 05:40.053
Give me the lamp.

05:41.763 --> 05:44.183
Dobby, stop!

05:46.353 --> 05:49.363
-Let me go.
-Get in there and keep quiet.

05:49.523 --> 05:53.573
-What the devil are you doing up here?
-l was just--

05:53.733 --> 05:56.493
You just ruined the punch line
of my Japanese golfer joke.

05:57.073 --> 05:58.493
Sorry.

06:00.033 --> 06:04.123
One more sound and you'll wish
you'd never been born, boy.

06:04.293 --> 06:08.083
-And fix that door.
-Yes, sir.

06:10.383 --> 06:12.003
See why l've got to go back?

06:12.173 --> 06:15.923
l don't belong here.
l belong in your world, at Hogwarts.

06:16.093 --> 06:20.723
-lt's the only place l've got friends.
-Friends who don't write to Harry Potter?

06:20.893 --> 06:23.813
Well, l expect they've been. . . .

06:23.973 --> 06:28.643
Hang on. How do you know
my friends haven't been writing to me?

06:29.063 --> 06:32.193
Harry Potter mustn't
be angry with Dobby.

06:32.363 --> 06:36.573
Dobby hoped if Harry Potter
thought his friends had forgotten him. . .

06:36.743 --> 06:40.413
. . .Harry Potter might not want
to go back to school, sir.

06:41.243 --> 06:46.003
-Give me those. Now.
-No!

06:58.303 --> 07:01.593
Dobby, get back here.

07:04.763 --> 07:08.103
Dobby, please, no.

07:08.273 --> 07:12.443
Harry Potter must say
he's not going back to school.

07:12.773 --> 07:15.233
l can't. Hogwarts is my home.

07:15.903 --> 07:21.493
Then Dobby must do it, sir,
for Harry Potter's own good.

07:21.663 --> 07:26.663
lt spread as far as the eye could see,
all over the floor of this building.

07:26.833 --> 07:28.793
One plumber said,
''Look at all that water. ''

07:28.953 --> 07:31.963
The second plumber said,
''Yes, and that's just the top of it. ''

07:43.723 --> 07:47.813
l'm so sorry. lt's my nephew.
He's very disturbed.

07:47.973 --> 07:52.313
Meeting strangers upsets him.
That's why l kept him upstairs.

08:04.033 --> 08:06.493
You're never going back to that school.

08:06.663 --> 08:11.713
You're never going to see those
freaky friends of yours again. Never!

08:57.883 --> 08:59.003
Hiya, Harry.

09:00.093 --> 09:04.553
Ron. Fred. George.
What are you all doing here?

09:04.723 --> 09:08.603
Rescuing you, of course.
Now, come on, get your trunk.

09:14.813 --> 09:17.023
You better stand back.

09:17.443 --> 09:19.573
Let's go.

09:24.323 --> 09:26.243
-What was that?
-What was it?

09:28.533 --> 09:30.743
Potter!

09:30.913 --> 09:32.583
Dad, what's going on?

09:35.833 --> 09:36.873
Go. Go. Go.

09:37.043 --> 09:38.083
Dad, hurry up.

09:39.923 --> 09:42.133
-Come on.
-Come on, Harry, hurry up.

09:44.093 --> 09:45.923
Petunia, he's escaping!

09:48.143 --> 09:49.643
-l've got you, Harry.
-Come here!

09:50.103 --> 09:51.933
-Let go of me!
-No, boy!

09:52.103 --> 09:55.103
You and that bloody pigeon
aren't going anywhere.

09:55.273 --> 09:56.893
-Get off!
-Drive!

09:57.063 --> 09:58.943
-Right.
-Right!

09:59.103 --> 10:00.773
No! No! No! No!

10:05.153 --> 10:06.953
Dad!

10:16.083 --> 10:17.583
Damn.

10:21.713 --> 10:25.593
By the way, Harry, happy birthday.

10:51.913 --> 10:53.703
Come on.

10:56.413 --> 10:58.333
Okay, come on.

10:59.163 --> 11:01.383
Okay, come on.

11:09.593 --> 11:13.683
-Think it'd be all right if we had some?
-Yeah, Mum will never know.

11:30.363 --> 11:33.573
lt's not much, but it's home.

11:33.743 --> 11:36.043
l think it's brilliant.

11:36.793 --> 11:40.543
Where have you been?

11:40.963 --> 11:44.003
Harry, how wonderful
to see you, dear.

11:44.173 --> 11:47.763
Beds empty. No note. Car gone.

11:47.923 --> 11:50.923
You could have died.
You could have been seen.

11:51.513 --> 11:54.143
Of course, l don't
blame you, Harry, dear.

11:54.303 --> 11:57.353
They were starving him, Mum.
There were bars on his window.

11:57.513 --> 12:02.273
Well, you best hope l don't put bars
on your window, Ronald Weasley.

12:02.443 --> 12:04.563
Come on, Harry,
time for a spot of breakfast.

12:05.733 --> 12:08.483
Here we are, Harry. Now, tuck in.

12:08.653 --> 12:12.243
That's it. There we go.

12:12.743 --> 12:16.243
-Mummy, have you seen my jumper?
-Yes, dear, it was on the cat.

12:16.833 --> 12:18.493
Hello.

12:22.833 --> 12:24.213
What did l do?

12:24.383 --> 12:28.963
Ginny. She's been talking about you
all summer. A bit annoying, really.

12:29.133 --> 12:31.763
-Morning, Weasleys.
-Morning, Dad.

12:32.723 --> 12:36.473
-What a night. Nine raids. Nine!
-Raids?

12:36.933 --> 12:40.603
Dad works in the Ministry of Magic,
in the Misuse of Muggle Artifacts Office.

12:40.933 --> 12:44.103
Dad loves Muggles,
thinks they're fascinating.

12:44.273 --> 12:46.483
Well, now.

12:48.403 --> 12:49.613
And who are you?

12:50.403 --> 12:53.953
Sorry, sir. l'm Harry, sir.
Harry Potter.

12:54.363 --> 12:57.243
Good Lord. Are you really?

12:57.783 --> 13:02.123
Well, Ron has told us all about you,
of course. When did he get here?

13:02.293 --> 13:03.793
This morning.

13:04.213 --> 13:09.173
Your sons flew that enchanted car
of yours to Surrey and back last night.

13:09.423 --> 13:12.803
Did you really? How did it go?

13:12.973 --> 13:17.803
l mean-- That was very wrong
indeed, boys. Very wrong of you.

13:19.143 --> 13:22.983
Now, Harry, you must know
all about Muggles.

13:23.233 --> 13:27.273
Tell me, what exactly
is the function of a rubber duck?

13:31.863 --> 13:34.613
Well, that'll be Errol with the post.

13:40.373 --> 13:43.163
Fetch it, will you, Percy, please?

13:43.503 --> 13:46.713
-Errol.
-He's always doing that.

13:48.383 --> 13:52.343
Look, it's our Hogwarts letters.
They've sent us Harry's as well.

13:52.503 --> 13:55.553
Dumbledore must know you're here.
Doesn't miss a trick, that man.

13:55.723 --> 13:57.683
-No.
-This lot won't come cheap.

13:57.843 --> 14:02.183
-The spell books alone are expensive.
-We'll manage.

14:02.893 --> 14:07.143
There's only one place we're going to
get all of this. Diagon Alley.

14:08.403 --> 14:09.773
Right.

14:09.943 --> 14:12.073
Here we are, Harry.
You go first, dear.

14:12.233 --> 14:15.193
But Harry's never traveled
by Floo powder before, Mum.

14:15.363 --> 14:16.403
Floo powder?

14:16.573 --> 14:20.873
You go first, Ron, so that Harry
can see how it's done. Yes.

14:21.493 --> 14:23.373
ln you go.

14:23.913 --> 14:25.413
That's it.

14:28.923 --> 14:30.633
Diagon Alley.

14:36.673 --> 14:40.183
You see? lt's quite easy, dear.
Don't be afraid. Come on.

14:41.933 --> 14:43.143
Come on.

14:43.313 --> 14:46.523
ln you go. That's it. Mind your head.

14:46.683 --> 14:50.103
That's right.
Now, take your Floo powder.

14:51.653 --> 14:54.113
That's it, very good.

14:54.273 --> 14:58.613
Now, don't forget to speak
very, very clearly.

15:00.453 --> 15:02.833
Diagonally.

15:09.293 --> 15:11.713
-What did he say, dear?
-Diagonally.

15:11.883 --> 15:12.963
l thought he did.

16:37.963 --> 16:44.263
-Not lost, are you, my dear?
-l'm fine, thank you. l was just going. . . .

16:44.433 --> 16:48.933
Come with us. We'll help you
find your way back.

16:49.473 --> 16:51.813
-No. Please--
-Harry?

16:51.983 --> 16:53.063
Hagrid!

16:53.233 --> 16:56.233
What do you think
you're doing down here? Come on.

17:02.033 --> 17:07.283
You're a mess, Harry. Skulking around
Knockturn Alley? Dodgy place.

17:07.453 --> 17:11.453
Don't want no one to see you there.
People will think you're up to no good.

17:11.623 --> 17:13.873
l was lost, l--

17:14.043 --> 17:17.003
Hang on. What were you
doing down there then?

17:17.173 --> 17:22.303
Me? l was. . . . l was looking
for Flesh-Eating Slug Repellent.

17:22.463 --> 17:25.383
They're ruining all the school cabbages.

17:30.813 --> 17:32.983
Harry. Hagrid.

17:33.183 --> 17:34.603
Hello, Hermione.

17:34.983 --> 17:37.603
-lt's so good to see you.
-lt's great to see you too.

17:38.273 --> 17:40.863
What did you do to your glasses?

17:41.033 --> 17:43.903
Oculus Reparo.

17:47.363 --> 17:50.123
l definitely need to remember that one.

17:50.283 --> 17:54.003
You'll be all right now then, Harry?
Right. l'll leave you to it.

17:54.163 --> 17:55.623
-Okay, bye.
-Thank you. Bye.

17:55.913 --> 17:57.793
Come on, everyone's been so worried.

18:08.513 --> 18:09.643
Harry.

18:09.803 --> 18:13.023
Thank goodness. We'd hoped
you'd only gone one grate too far.

18:13.183 --> 18:16.023
Ladies and gentlemen,
Mr. Gilderoy Lockhart.

18:16.193 --> 18:18.483
Here he is.

18:22.483 --> 18:24.113
Mum fancies him.

18:24.283 --> 18:27.533
Make way there, please.
Let me by, madam. Thank you.

18:27.743 --> 18:31.163
Excuse me, little girl.
This is for the Daily Prophet.

18:35.333 --> 18:38.213
lt can't be. Harry Potter?

18:39.753 --> 18:41.633
Harry Potter!

18:41.793 --> 18:43.003
Excuse me, madam.

18:45.013 --> 18:48.843
Nice big smile, Harry.
Together, you and l rate the front page.

18:49.013 --> 18:52.183
Ladies and gentlemen,
what an extraordinary moment this is.

18:52.603 --> 18:55.773
When young Harry stepped
into Flourish and Blotts this morning. . .

18:55.933 --> 19:00.023
. . .to purchase my autobiography,
Magical Me. . .

19:03.523 --> 19:06.403
. . .which, incidentally,
is currently celebrating. . .

19:06.573 --> 19:11.413
. . .its 27th week atop
the Daily Prophet bestseller list. . .

19:11.573 --> 19:16.083
. . .he had no idea that he would,
in fact, be leaving. . .

19:17.253 --> 19:22.173
. . .with my entire collected works. . .

19:22.753 --> 19:24.963
. . .free of charge.

19:27.133 --> 19:29.383
Now, ladies?

19:29.593 --> 19:32.723
Harry, now you give me those,
and l'll get them signed.

19:32.893 --> 19:36.393
All of you wait outside.
That's it.

19:45.693 --> 19:48.193
l'll bet you loved that,
didn't you, Potter?

19:48.363 --> 19:52.873
Famous Harry Potter. Can't go into a
bookshop without making the front page.

19:53.493 --> 19:55.203
Leave him alone.

19:55.373 --> 19:58.873
Look, Potter.
You've got yourself a girlfriend.

19:59.043 --> 20:03.083
Now, now, Draco, play nicely.

20:03.503 --> 20:04.713
Mr. Potter.

20:07.173 --> 20:11.133
Lucius Malfoy. We meet at last.

20:11.303 --> 20:13.513
Forgive me.

20:14.893 --> 20:16.933
Your scar is legend.

20:17.473 --> 20:19.733
As, of course, is the wizard
who gave it to you.

20:20.063 --> 20:22.233
Voldemort killed my parents.

20:24.313 --> 20:27.783
He was nothing more than a murderer.

20:28.823 --> 20:31.743
You must be very brave
to mention his name.

20:32.403 --> 20:33.743
Or very foolish.

20:34.163 --> 20:37.703
Fear of a name only increases
fear of the thing itself.

20:39.293 --> 20:42.583
And you must be Miss Granger.

20:45.423 --> 20:49.713
Yes, Draco has told me
all about you. And your parents.

20:54.343 --> 20:57.813
Muggles, aren't they?

21:00.773 --> 21:05.853
Let me see.
Red hair, vacant expressions. . .

21:07.273 --> 21:10.613
. . .tatty, secondhand book.

21:10.823 --> 21:14.153
You must be the Weasleys.

21:14.613 --> 21:16.623
lt's mad in here.
Let's go outside.

21:16.783 --> 21:20.493
-Well, well, well. Weasley senior.
-Lucius.

21:20.703 --> 21:25.373
Busy time at the Ministry, Arthur,
all those extra raids?

21:25.543 --> 21:27.883
l do hope they're paying you overtime. . .

21:28.043 --> 21:31.213
. . .but judging by the state of this,
l'd say not.

21:33.013 --> 21:36.763
What's the use in being a disgrace
to the name of wizard. . .

21:36.933 --> 21:39.013
. . .if they don't even pay you well for it?

21:39.313 --> 21:44.313
We have a very different idea about what
disgraces the name of wizard, Malfoy.

21:44.563 --> 21:46.353
Clearly.

21:48.443 --> 21:52.153
Associating with Muggles.

21:56.363 --> 22:00.953
And l thought your family
could sink no lower.

22:04.253 --> 22:07.043
l'll see you at work.

22:11.213 --> 22:13.553
See you at school.

22:21.393 --> 22:24.063
-1 0:58, come on.
-The train will be leaving any moment.

22:24.223 --> 22:27.523
Fred, George, Percy, you first.

22:33.113 --> 22:34.743
Okay.

22:40.783 --> 22:42.533
After you, dear.

22:44.703 --> 22:47.923
Come on, Ginny,
we'll get you a seat. Hurry.

22:49.213 --> 22:51.293
Let's go.

23:05.223 --> 23:08.393
-What do you two think you're doing?
-Sorry.

23:08.813 --> 23:11.813
Lost control of the trolley.

23:13.153 --> 23:15.483
-Why can't we get through?
-l don't know.

23:15.653 --> 23:19.033
The gateway has sealed
itself for some reason.

23:20.413 --> 23:24.333
The train leaves at exactly 1 1 :00.
We've missed it.

23:24.493 --> 23:27.873
Harry, if we can't get through. . .

23:28.163 --> 23:30.833
. . .maybe Mum and Dad can't get back.

23:31.793 --> 23:35.253
Maybe we should just go
and wait by the car.

23:36.303 --> 23:37.633
The car.

23:49.143 --> 23:51.313
Ron, l should tell you. . .

23:51.483 --> 23:55.273
. . .most Muggles aren't accustomed
to seeing a flying car.

23:55.443 --> 23:56.533
Right.

23:56.823 --> 23:57.863
Okay.

24:15.173 --> 24:18.463
Oh, no! The lnvisibility Booster
must be faulty.

24:18.923 --> 24:22.053
Come on, then. Let's go lower.
We need to find the train.

24:22.223 --> 24:23.513
Okay.

24:34.443 --> 24:36.483
All we need to do is catch up
with the train.

24:36.653 --> 24:38.323
We can't be far behind.

24:40.323 --> 24:43.033
-Do you hear that?
-We must be getting close.

24:43.413 --> 24:45.573
Hold on.

25:11.893 --> 25:14.063
Harry!

25:16.693 --> 25:18.523
Hold on!

25:21.863 --> 25:24.363
Take my hand!

25:28.623 --> 25:29.873
Hold on!

25:30.043 --> 25:33.623
l'm trying. Your hand's all sweaty.

25:46.223 --> 25:49.513
-l think we found the train.
-Yeah.

26:06.203 --> 26:07.453
Welcome home.

26:23.593 --> 26:24.803
Up! Up!

26:25.763 --> 26:27.933
lt's not working!

26:31.853 --> 26:34.433
Up! Ron, mind that tree!

26:37.693 --> 26:39.813
Stop! Stop! Stop!

27:02.923 --> 27:07.553
-My wand. Look at my wand.
-Be thankful it's not your neck.

27:09.183 --> 27:12.183
-What's happening?
-l don't know.

27:47.633 --> 27:49.763
Come on, go! Fast!

28:24.133 --> 28:26.923
Scabbers, you're okay.

28:28.423 --> 28:30.473
The car!

28:45.943 --> 28:47.783
Dad's gonna kill me.

28:56.333 --> 28:58.663
See you, Hedwig.

29:00.003 --> 29:02.333
So a house-elf shows up
in my bedroom. . .

29:02.503 --> 29:05.463
. . .we can't get through the barrier
to platform 9 3/4. . .

29:05.633 --> 29:08.883
. . .we almost get killed by a tree. . . .

29:09.053 --> 29:12.593
Clearly someone doesn't want me
here this year.

29:16.183 --> 29:19.143
Well, take a good look, lads.

29:19.313 --> 29:23.233
This night might well be
the last you spend in this castle.

29:26.023 --> 29:29.533
Oh, dear, we are in trouble.

29:29.823 --> 29:35.993
You were seen by no less
than seven Muggles.

29:36.453 --> 29:39.203
Do you have any idea
how serious this is?

29:39.913 --> 29:43.753
You have risked
the exposure of our world.

29:44.423 --> 29:47.333
Not to mention the damage you
inflicted on a Whomping Willow. . .

29:47.503 --> 29:50.673
. . .that's been on these grounds
since before you were born.

29:51.133 --> 29:54.683
Honestly, Professor Snape,
l think it did more damage to us.

29:54.843 --> 29:56.013
Silence.

29:58.013 --> 30:04.393
l assure you that were you in Slytherin,
and your fate rested with me. . .

30:04.563 --> 30:08.363
. . .the both of you would be
on the train home tonight.

30:09.523 --> 30:11.783
-As it is--
-They are not.

30:13.993 --> 30:18.033
Professor Dumbledore.
Professor McGonagall.

30:18.413 --> 30:19.913
Headmaster. . .

30:20.083 --> 30:24.873
. . .these boys have flouted the Decree
for the Restriction of Underage Wizardry.

30:25.043 --> 30:28.963
-As such--
-l am well aware of our bylaws. . .

30:29.133 --> 30:32.003
. . .having written
quite a few of them myself.

30:32.383 --> 30:35.593
However, as head of Gryffindor house. . .

30:35.763 --> 30:40.763
. . .it is for Professor McGonagall
to determine the appropriate action.

30:41.223 --> 30:43.393
We'll go and get our stuff, then.

30:43.563 --> 30:46.023
What are you
talking about, Mr. Weasley?

30:46.193 --> 30:48.403
You're going to expel us, aren't you?

30:49.943 --> 30:53.073
Not today, Mr. Weasley. . .

30:53.233 --> 30:58.243
. . .but l must impress on both of you
the seriousness of what you have done.

30:58.783 --> 31:03.413
l will be writing to your families tonight,
and you will both receive detention.

31:27.773 --> 31:30.273
Morning, everyone.

31:30.943 --> 31:33.483
-Good morning, everyone.
-Good morning, Professor Sprout.

31:33.653 --> 31:37.953
Welcome to Greenhouse Three,
second years. Gather around, everyone.

31:38.113 --> 31:40.953
Today we're going to re-pot Mandrakes.

31:41.123 --> 31:45.123
Who here can tell me
the properties of the Mandrake root?

31:45.293 --> 31:47.123
Yes, Miss Granger?

31:47.293 --> 31:49.623
Mandrake, or Mandragora. . .

31:49.793 --> 31:54.803
. . .is used to return those who have been
Petrified to their original state.

31:54.963 --> 31:59.973
lt's also dangerous. The Mandrake's
cry is fatal to anyone who hears it.

32:00.133 --> 32:02.973
Excellent. Ten points to Gryffindor.

32:03.143 --> 32:05.813
As our Mandrakes
are still only seedlings. . .

32:05.973 --> 32:07.893
. . .their cries won't kill you yet.

32:08.063 --> 32:11.853
But they could knock you out for hours,
which is why l have given you earmuffs. . .

32:12.023 --> 32:13.523
. . .for auditory protection.

32:13.693 --> 32:18.153
So could you please put them on,
right away? Quickly.

32:18.323 --> 32:21.113
Flaps tight down,
and watch me closely.

32:21.283 --> 32:24.283
You grasp your Mandrake firmly.

32:24.453 --> 32:27.453
You pull it sharply up out of the pot.

32:31.713 --> 32:33.633
Got it? And. . .

32:33.833 --> 32:35.963
. . .now you dunk it down
into the other pot. . .

32:36.133 --> 32:40.843
. . .and pour a little sprinkling of soil
to keep him warm.

32:44.473 --> 32:47.683
Longbottom's been neglecting
his earmuffs.

32:48.103 --> 32:52.143
-No, ma'am, he's just fainted.
-Yes, well, just leave him there.

32:52.523 --> 32:56.073
Right, on we go.
Plenty of pots to go around.

32:56.233 --> 32:59.823
Grasp your Mandrake and pull it up.

33:14.753 --> 33:18.553
-There's Nearly Headless Nick.
-Hello, Percy, Miss Clearwater.

33:18.713 --> 33:21.263
Hello, Sir Nicholas.

33:32.733 --> 33:36.023
Say it. l'm doomed.

33:36.863 --> 33:38.773
-You're doomed.
-Hi, Harry.

33:41.033 --> 33:43.743
l'm Colin Creevey. l'm in Gryffindor too.

33:43.903 --> 33:45.533
Hi, Colin. Nice to meet you.

33:46.073 --> 33:47.913
Ron, is that your owl?

34:02.633 --> 34:05.303
Bloody bird's a menace.

34:09.513 --> 34:11.023
Oh, no.

34:11.183 --> 34:14.643
Look, everyone.
Weasley's got himself a Howler.

34:16.103 --> 34:21.363
Go on, Ron. l ignored one
from my gran once. lt was horrible.

34:28.533 --> 34:30.413
Ronald Weasley!

34:33.043 --> 34:39.133
How dare you steal that car!
I am absolutely disgusted!

34:39.423 --> 34:42.003
Your father's now facing
an inquiry at work...

34:42.173 --> 34:44.553
...and it's entirely your fault!

34:45.013 --> 34:48.893
If you put another toe out of line...

34:49.053 --> 34:52.313
... we'll bring you straight home!

34:53.103 --> 34:56.603
And, Ginny, dear, congratulations
on making Gryffindor.

34:56.773 --> 35:00.483
Your father and I are so proud.

35:18.753 --> 35:25.173
Let me introduce you to your new
Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

35:25.343 --> 35:26.883
Me.

35:27.053 --> 35:29.593
Gilderoy Lockhart. . .

35:29.763 --> 35:33.063
. . .Order of Merlin, Third Class. . .

35:33.223 --> 35:36.563
. . .honorary member
of the Dark Force Defense League. . .

35:36.733 --> 35:39.653
. . .and five times winner. . .

35:39.983 --> 35:45.863
. . .of Witch Weekly's
Most-Charming-Smile Award.

35:46.243 --> 35:47.743
But l don't talk about that.

35:47.903 --> 35:52.453
l didn't get rid of the Bandon Banshee
by smiling at him.

35:56.203 --> 35:59.043
Now, be warned.

35:59.333 --> 36:01.383
lt is my job to arm you. . .

36:01.543 --> 36:06.883
. . .against the foulest creatures
known to wizardkind.

36:07.723 --> 36:11.303
You may find yourselves facing
your worst fears in this room.

36:11.473 --> 36:15.513
Know only that no harm
can befall you whilst l am here.

36:15.683 --> 36:18.603
l must ask you not to scream.

36:18.773 --> 36:21.353
lt might provoke them.

36:24.823 --> 36:26.363
Cornish pixies?

36:26.533 --> 36:29.573
Freshly caught Cornish pixies.

36:30.363 --> 36:32.493
Laugh if you will, Mr. Finnegan. . .

36:32.663 --> 36:36.833
. . .but pixies can be
devilishly tricky little blighters.

36:36.993 --> 36:39.913
Let's see what you make of them.

36:44.253 --> 36:47.503
Come on now, round them up.
They're only pixies.

37:03.273 --> 37:07.403
-You just stay there!
-Please, get me down!

37:09.743 --> 37:12.203
-Get off me!
-Stop. Hold still!

37:13.823 --> 37:17.033
Peskipiksi Pesternomi!

37:37.013 --> 37:41.313
l'll ask you three to just nip
the rest of them back into their cage.

37:43.063 --> 37:45.233
What do we do now?

37:46.693 --> 37:48.193
Immobulus!

37:57.703 --> 37:59.953
Why is it always me?

38:06.293 --> 38:09.003
l spent the summer devising
a whole new Quidditch program.

38:09.173 --> 38:12.843
We're gonna train earlier,
harder and longer.

38:13.013 --> 38:16.303
What--? l don't believe it.

38:19.103 --> 38:21.813
-Where you think you're going, Flint?
-Quidditch practice.

38:21.973 --> 38:26.353
-l booked the pitch for Gryffindor today.
-Easy, Wood. l've got a note.

38:27.773 --> 38:29.983
l smell trouble.

38:30.573 --> 38:34.113
''l, Professor Severus Snape,
do hereby give the Slytherin team. . .

38:34.283 --> 38:37.783
. . .permission to practice today, owing
to the need to train their new Seeker. ''

38:37.953 --> 38:40.623
You've got a new Seeker. Who?

38:44.583 --> 38:47.213
-Malfoy?
-That's right.

38:47.373 --> 38:50.173
And that's not all
that's new this year.

38:51.003 --> 38:54.423
Those are Nimbus 2001 s.
How did you get those?

38:54.593 --> 38:56.683
A gift from Draco's father.

38:56.843 --> 39:00.603
You see, Weasley, unlike some,
my father can afford the best.

39:00.763 --> 39:03.773
At least no one on the Gryffindor team
had to buy their way in.

39:03.933 --> 39:06.853
They got in on pure talent.

39:10.063 --> 39:13.943
No one asked your opinion,
you filthy little Mudblood.

39:16.453 --> 39:19.913
You'll pay for that one, Malfoy.
Eat slugs!

39:27.463 --> 39:29.333
You okay, Ron?

39:32.343 --> 39:34.133
Say something.

39:40.393 --> 39:44.893
-Wow! Can you turn him around, Harry?
-No, Colin, get out of the way.

39:45.813 --> 39:47.853
Let's take him to Hagrid's.

39:48.023 --> 39:50.153
He'll know what to do.

39:59.033 --> 40:02.413
This calls for
a specialist's equipment.

40:06.163 --> 40:09.753
Nothing to do but wait till it stops,
l'm afraid.

40:10.423 --> 40:13.593
-Okay.
-Better out than in.

40:14.173 --> 40:19.513
-Who was Ron trying to curse, anyway?
-Malfoy. He called Hermione. . . .

40:20.723 --> 40:24.143
Well, l don't know
exactly what it means.

40:28.103 --> 40:30.313
He called me a Mudblood.

40:30.483 --> 40:33.153
-He did not.
-What's a Mudblood?

40:33.523 --> 40:38.073
lt means ''dirty blood. '' Mudblood's a foul
name for someone who's Muggle-born.

40:38.243 --> 40:42.493
Someone with non-magic parents.
Someone like me.

40:42.993 --> 40:47.123
lt's not a term one usually hears
in civilized conversation.

40:48.293 --> 40:53.083
See, the thing is, Harry, there are
some wizards, like the Malfoy family. . .

40:53.253 --> 40:57.923
. . .who think they're better than everyone
else because they're pure-blood.

40:58.093 --> 40:59.723
That's horrible.

41:02.723 --> 41:04.053
lt's disgusting.

41:04.223 --> 41:07.723
And it's codswallop to boot.
Dirty blood.

41:07.893 --> 41:11.273
Why, there isn't a wizard alive today
that's not half-blood or less.

41:11.443 --> 41:15.983
More to the point, they've yet to think
of a spell that our Hermione can't do.

41:16.153 --> 41:18.363
Come here.

41:19.493 --> 41:25.953
Don't you think on it, Hermione.
Don't you think on it for one minute.

41:33.713 --> 41:36.753
Harry, Harry, Harry.

41:36.923 --> 41:39.173
Can you possibly imagine. . .

41:39.343 --> 41:42.553
. . .a better way to serve detention. . .

41:43.183 --> 41:45.893
. . .than by helping me
to answer my fan mail?

41:46.053 --> 41:47.473
Not really.

41:47.643 --> 41:54.023
Fame is a fickle friend, Harry.
Celebrity is as celebrity does.

41:54.193 --> 41:56.113
Remember that.

41:59.863 --> 42:02.033
Come.

42:02.193 --> 42:04.323
Come...

42:05.573 --> 42:08.453
... to me.

42:11.753 --> 42:14.293
-What?
-Sorry?

42:16.543 --> 42:18.503
That voice.

42:18.673 --> 42:20.213
Voice?

42:23.763 --> 42:28.393
-Didn't you hear it?
-What are you talking about, Harry?

42:29.013 --> 42:32.603
l think you're getting
a bit drowsy.

42:32.773 --> 42:36.853
And great Scott, no wonder. Look at the
time. We've been here nearly four hours.

42:37.153 --> 42:40.523
Spooky how the time flies
when one is having fun.

42:45.493 --> 42:48.033
Spooky.

42:51.083 --> 42:53.203
Blood.

42:53.373 --> 42:56.923
I smell blood.

42:57.083 --> 43:00.173
Let me rip you.

43:00.343 --> 43:03.923
Let me kill you.

43:05.763 --> 43:07.223
Kill!

43:08.143 --> 43:09.473
Kill!

43:10.183 --> 43:12.103
-Kill!
-Harry!

43:12.263 --> 43:14.773
-Did you hear it?
-Hear what?

43:14.933 --> 43:18.353
-That voice.
-Voice? What voice?

43:18.523 --> 43:22.483
l heard it first in Lockhart's office.
And then again just--

43:22.783 --> 43:24.863
It's time.

43:25.033 --> 43:28.243
lt's moving.
l think it's going to kill.

43:29.203 --> 43:33.163
-Kill?
-Harry, wait! Not so fast!

43:58.733 --> 44:00.813
Strange.

44:01.313 --> 44:05.823
-l've never seen spiders act like that.
-l don't like spiders.

44:09.953 --> 44:11.993
What's that?

44:15.453 --> 44:20.003
''The Chamber of Secrets has been
opened. Enemies of the Heir, beware. ''

44:20.173 --> 44:22.423
lt's written in blood.

44:25.343 --> 44:27.513
Oh, no.

44:32.223 --> 44:34.513
lt's Filch's cat.

44:35.013 --> 44:37.313
lt's Mrs. Norris.

44:53.373 --> 44:56.083
''Enemies of the Heir, beware. ''

44:57.583 --> 44:59.963
You'll be next, Mudbloods.

45:00.123 --> 45:05.293
What's going on here?
Go on. Make way, make way.

45:06.753 --> 45:08.593
Potter?

45:08.763 --> 45:10.883
What are you. . .?

45:14.223 --> 45:16.513
Mrs. Norris?

45:18.023 --> 45:22.193
-You've murdered my cat.
-No. No.

45:22.563 --> 45:23.853
l'll kill you.

45:26.193 --> 45:29.033
-l'll kill you!
-Argus!

45:30.403 --> 45:32.573
Argus, l. . . .

45:34.573 --> 45:39.203
Everyone will proceed
to their dormitories immediately.

45:39.913 --> 45:41.913
Everyone except. . .

45:42.713 --> 45:44.923
. . .you three.

45:47.043 --> 45:49.803
Ravenclaws, follow me.

45:51.673 --> 45:55.553
She's not dead, Argus.
She has been Petrified.

45:55.723 --> 45:58.563
Thought so.
So unlucky l wasn't there.

45:58.723 --> 46:01.933
l know exactly the countercurse
that could've spared her.

46:04.273 --> 46:06.903
But how she has been Petrified,
l cannot say.

46:07.153 --> 46:09.863
Ask him.
lt's him that's done it.

46:10.033 --> 46:12.743
You saw what he wrote on the wall.

46:12.903 --> 46:16.993
lt's not true, sir. l swear.
l never touched Mrs. Norris.

46:17.163 --> 46:21.623
-Rubbish.
-lf l might, headmaster?

46:22.083 --> 46:26.883
Perhaps Potter and his friends were just
in the wrong place at the wrong time.

46:27.383 --> 46:29.293
However. . .

46:29.633 --> 46:32.593
. . .the circumstances are suspicious.

46:32.763 --> 46:37.393
l, for one, don't recall
seeing Potter at dinner.

46:37.553 --> 46:39.813
l'm afraid that's my doing, Severus.

46:39.973 --> 46:43.393
You see, Harry was helping me
answer my fan mail.

46:43.563 --> 46:46.853
That's why Ron and l
went looking for him, professor.

46:47.023 --> 46:49.773
We'd just found him when he said. . . .

46:52.033 --> 46:55.863
-Yes, Miss Granger?
-When l said l wasn't hungry.

46:57.243 --> 47:01.243
We were heading back to the common
room when we found Mrs. Norris.

47:03.583 --> 47:09.133
-lnnocent until proven guilty, Severus.
-My cat has been Petrified.

47:09.963 --> 47:15.803
-l want to see some punishment!
-We will be able to cure her, Argus.

47:16.723 --> 47:21.513
As l understand it, Madam Sprout
has a very healthy growth of Mandrake.

47:21.683 --> 47:26.103
When matured, a potion will be made
which will revive Mrs. Norris.

47:26.443 --> 47:28.153
And in the meantime. . .

47:28.693 --> 47:32.693
. . .l strongly recommend caution. . .

47:33.363 --> 47:35.363
. . .to all.

47:46.373 --> 47:49.833
-lt's a bit strange, isn't it?
-Strange?

47:50.003 --> 47:52.753
You hear this voice,
a voice only you can hear. . .

47:52.923 --> 47:57.633
. . .and then Mrs. Norris turns up
Petrified. lt's just strange.

47:57.803 --> 48:01.053
Do you think l should have told them?
Dumbledore and the others, l mean?

48:01.223 --> 48:02.683
Are you mad?

48:02.853 --> 48:08.353
No, Harry. Even in the wizarding world,
hearing voices isn't a good sign.

48:10.443 --> 48:12.823
She's right, you know.

48:17.153 --> 48:19.493
Could l have your attention,
please?

48:20.033 --> 48:25.543
Right. Now, today,
we will be transforming animals. . .

48:25.703 --> 48:28.083
. . .into water goblets.

48:29.003 --> 48:30.673
Like so.

48:30.833 --> 48:35.753
One, two, three.
Vera Verto.

48:39.303 --> 48:43.223
Now it's your turn.
Who would like to go first?

48:43.803 --> 48:48.773
Mr. Weasley.
''One, two, three. Vera Verto. ''

48:52.353 --> 48:54.443
Vera Verto!

49:00.573 --> 49:03.243
That wand needs replacing,
Mr. Weasley.

49:04.583 --> 49:06.743
-Yes, Miss Granger?
-Professor. . .

49:06.913 --> 49:11.123
. . .l was wondering if you could tell us
about the Chamber of Secrets.

49:17.303 --> 49:18.553
Very well.

49:20.053 --> 49:22.053
You all know, of course. . .

49:22.223 --> 49:26.103
. . .that Hogwarts was founded
over a thousand years ago. . .

49:26.263 --> 49:30.683
. . .by the four greatest witches
and wizards of the age:

49:30.853 --> 49:34.613
Godric Gryffindor,
Helga Hufflepuff. . .

49:34.773 --> 49:40.403
. . .Rowena Ravenclaw
and Salazar Slytherin.

49:41.073 --> 49:47.083
Now, three of the founders
coexisted quite harmoniously.

49:47.243 --> 49:50.293
-One did not.
-Three guesses who.

49:51.003 --> 49:53.463
Salazar Slytherin wished to be
more selective. . .

49:53.623 --> 49:56.793
. . .about the students admitted
to Hogwarts.

49:56.963 --> 50:01.553
He believed magical learning should
be kept within all-magic families.

50:01.723 --> 50:03.843
ln other words, pure-bloods.

50:04.223 --> 50:09.563
Unable to sway the others,
he decided to leave the school.

50:10.393 --> 50:12.643
Now, according to legend. . .

50:12.813 --> 50:16.523
. . .Slytherin had built
a hidden chamber in this castle. . .

50:16.693 --> 50:20.363
. . .known as the Chamber of Secrets.

50:20.533 --> 50:24.953
Though, shortly before departing,
he sealed it. . .

50:25.113 --> 50:29.243
. . .until that time when his own
true Heir returned to the school.

50:29.413 --> 50:31.793
The Heir alone. . .

50:31.953 --> 50:34.623
. . .would be able to open the Chamber. . .

50:34.793 --> 50:39.553
. . .and unleash the horror within,
and by so doing. . .

50:39.713 --> 50:43.093
. . .purge the school
of all those who. . .

50:43.263 --> 50:48.263
. . .in Slytherin's view,
were unworthy to study magic.

50:48.893 --> 50:51.023
Muggle-borns.

50:52.063 --> 50:55.693
Naturally, the school
has been searched many times.

50:55.853 --> 50:59.323
No such chamber has been found.

50:59.903 --> 51:04.573
Professor? What exactly does legend
tell us lies within the Chamber?

51:05.403 --> 51:07.993
The Chamber is said to be home
to something. . .

51:08.163 --> 51:11.743
. . .that only the Heir of Slytherin
can control.

51:12.373 --> 51:16.003
lt is said to be the home. . .

51:16.173 --> 51:17.793
. . .of a monster.

51:23.553 --> 51:27.223
Do you think it's true? Do you think
there really is a Chamber of Secrets?

51:27.383 --> 51:31.603
Yes. Couldn't you tell? McGonagall's
worried. All the teachers are.

51:31.763 --> 51:35.603
lf there really is a Chamber of Secrets,
and it has been opened, that means--

51:35.773 --> 51:39.733
The Heir of Slytherin has returned
to Hogwarts. The question is, who is it?

51:39.903 --> 51:44.283
Let's think. Who do we know who
thinks all Muggle-borns are scum?

51:44.443 --> 51:47.113
-lf you're talking about Malfoy--
-Of course. You heard him.

51:47.283 --> 51:48.993
''You'll be next, Mudbloods. ''

51:49.163 --> 51:51.783
l heard him.
But Malfoy, the Heir of Slytherin?

51:51.953 --> 51:55.123
Maybe Ron's right, Hermione.
l mean, look at his family.

51:55.293 --> 51:58.083
The whole lot of them have been
in Slytherin for centuries.

51:58.253 --> 52:01.673
Crabbe and Goyle must know.
Maybe we could trick them into telling.

52:02.133 --> 52:06.303
Even they aren't that thick.
But there might be another way.

52:06.473 --> 52:08.303
Mind you, it would be difficult.

52:08.473 --> 52:11.513
Not to mention we'd be breaking
about 50 school rules. . .

52:11.683 --> 52:16.143
. . .and it'll be dangerous.
Very dangerous.

52:22.983 --> 52:25.443
Here it is.
The Polyjuice Potion.

52:25.613 --> 52:28.323
''Properly brewed, the Polyjuice Potion
allows the drinker. . .

52:28.493 --> 52:32.743
. . .to transform himself temporarily
into the physical form of another. ''

52:32.913 --> 52:36.703
You mean if Harry and l drink that stuff,
we'll turn into Crabbe and Goyle?

52:36.873 --> 52:40.253
-Wicked! Malfoy will tell us anything.
-Exactly.

52:40.423 --> 52:44.293
But it's tricky. l've never seen
a more complicated potion.

52:44.463 --> 52:47.553
-How long will it take to make?
-A month.

52:47.923 --> 52:49.383
A month?

52:49.553 --> 52:53.393
But, Hermione,
if Malfoy is the Heir of Slytherin. . .

52:53.553 --> 52:56.773
. . .he could attack half
the Muggle-borns in the school by then.

52:56.933 --> 52:58.853
l know.

52:59.023 --> 53:01.853
But it's the only plan we've got.

53:51.533 --> 53:54.243
Another goal for Slytherin!

53:55.663 --> 53:58.953
They lead Gryffindor 90 to 30.

54:00.123 --> 54:01.713
Yeah!

54:01.963 --> 54:03.753
Yeah!

54:27.983 --> 54:30.323
All right there, Scarhead?

54:36.453 --> 54:38.953
Watch yourself, Harry!

54:39.333 --> 54:41.123
Wood, look out!

54:54.803 --> 54:57.643
Blimey! Harry's got himself
a rogue Bludger.

54:57.803 --> 54:59.563
That's been tampered with, that has.

55:00.603 --> 55:01.643
l'll stop it.

55:01.813 --> 55:06.403
No! Even with a proper wand,
it's too risky. You could hit Harry.

55:31.463 --> 55:34.053
Training for the ballet, Potter?

56:05.043 --> 56:07.253
You'll never catch me, Potter.

57:38.053 --> 57:39.133
Let's go.

57:39.303 --> 57:44.513
Harry Potter has caught the Snitch.
Gryffindor wins!

57:50.813 --> 57:52.853
Finite Incantatem!

57:59.943 --> 58:01.283
-Thank you.
-Are you okay?

58:01.453 --> 58:03.533
No. l think my arm is broken.

58:03.703 --> 58:07.493
Not to worry, Harry. l will fix
that arm of yours straightaway.

58:07.663 --> 58:10.623
-Not you.
-Boy doesn't know what he's saying.

58:10.793 --> 58:14.333
This won't hurt a bit.

58:20.423 --> 58:23.433
Brackium Emendo!

58:31.483 --> 58:34.563
Yes, well,
that can sometimes happen. . .

58:34.733 --> 58:36.983
. . .but the point is. . .

58:38.363 --> 58:42.493
. . .you can no longer feel any pain, and,
very clearly, the bones are not broken.

58:42.653 --> 58:45.323
Broken? There's no bones left.

58:47.033 --> 58:48.993
Much more flexible, though.

58:51.453 --> 58:55.373
Mr. Malfoy, stop making such a fuss.
You can go. Out of my way.

58:55.543 --> 58:57.503
Should have been brought
straight to me.

58:57.673 --> 59:00.213
l can mend bones in a heartbeat,
but growing them back. . . .

59:00.383 --> 59:01.883
You will be able to, won't you?

59:02.053 --> 59:05.183
l'll be able to, certainly.
But it'll be painful.

59:05.803 --> 59:10.473
You're in for a rough night, Potter.
Regrowing bones is a nasty business.

59:13.393 --> 59:16.403
What do you expect?
Pumpkin juice?

59:23.033 --> 59:24.783
Kill.

59:25.613 --> 59:27.163
Kill.

59:32.543 --> 59:35.753
Time to kill.

59:41.883 --> 59:42.923
Hello.

59:44.723 --> 59:45.763
Dobby?

59:45.923 --> 59:48.263
Harry Potter should have listened
to Dobby.

59:48.723 --> 59:52.433
Harry Potter should have gone back home
when he missed the train.

59:52.603 --> 59:57.233
lt was you. You stopped the barrier
from letting Ron and me through.

59:57.523 --> 01:00:00.483
lndeed. Yes, sir.

01:00:01.483 --> 01:00:06.533
-You nearly got Ron and me expelled.
-At least you would be away from here.

01:00:06.703 --> 01:00:09.373
Harry Potter must go home.

01:00:09.533 --> 01:00:13.123
Dobby thought his Bludger would be
enough to make Harry Potter see--

01:00:13.293 --> 01:00:16.663
Your Bludger? You made
that Bludger chase after me?

01:00:16.833 --> 01:00:20.423
Dobby feels most aggrieved, sir.

01:00:20.583 --> 01:00:24.213
Dobby had to iron his hands.

01:00:26.423 --> 01:00:31.013
You better clear off before my bones
come back, or l might strangle you.

01:00:33.643 --> 01:00:35.643
Dobby is used to death threats, sir.

01:00:35.813 --> 01:00:38.853
Dobby gets them five times a day
at home.

01:00:39.023 --> 01:00:41.813
l don't suppose you could tell me
why you're trying to kill me?

01:00:42.113 --> 01:00:45.993
Not kill you, sir.
Never kill you.

01:00:46.153 --> 01:00:49.493
Dobby remembers how it was
before Harry Potter triumphed. . .

01:00:49.663 --> 01:00:52.783
. . .over He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named.

01:00:52.953 --> 01:00:56.663
We house-elves were
treated like vermin, sir.

01:00:56.833 --> 01:01:02.253
Of course, Dobby is still
treated like vermin.

01:01:11.593 --> 01:01:14.223
Why do you wear that thing, Dobby?

01:01:14.393 --> 01:01:19.523
This, sir? lt is a mark
of the house-elf's enslavement.

01:01:19.693 --> 01:01:24.823
Dobby can only be freed if his master
presents him with clothes.

01:01:26.943 --> 01:01:28.323
Listen.

01:01:28.493 --> 01:01:30.033
Listen!

01:01:30.203 --> 01:01:33.913
Terrible things are
about to happen at Hogwarts.

01:01:34.533 --> 01:01:36.993
Harry Potter must not stay here. . .

01:01:37.163 --> 01:01:41.713
. . .now that history
is to repeat itself.

01:01:41.873 --> 01:01:45.343
Repeat itself? You mean
this has happened before?

01:01:45.503 --> 01:01:47.503
l shouldn't have said that.

01:01:51.223 --> 01:01:54.393
-Bad Dobby! Bad!
-Stop it!

01:01:54.553 --> 01:01:56.223
Stop it, Dobby!

01:01:57.893 --> 01:02:01.733
Tell me. When did this happen before?
Who's doing it now?

01:02:01.893 --> 01:02:07.113
Dobby cannot say, sir. Dobby
only wants Harry Potter to be safe.

01:02:07.273 --> 01:02:10.193
No, Dobby. Tell me.
Who is it?

01:02:22.043 --> 01:02:23.123
Put him here.

01:02:27.713 --> 01:02:30.633
-What happened?
-There's been another attack.

01:02:30.803 --> 01:02:36.603
l think he's been Petrified,
Madam Pomfrey.

01:02:37.393 --> 01:02:42.103
Look. Perhaps he managed
to take a picture of his attacker.

01:02:50.193 --> 01:02:52.953
What can this mean, Albus?

01:02:53.113 --> 01:02:55.073
lt means. . .

01:02:55.453 --> 01:02:58.203
. . .that our students
are in great danger.

01:02:58.373 --> 01:03:01.793
-What should l tell the staff?
-The truth.

01:03:02.043 --> 01:03:05.833
Tell them Hogwarts
is no longer safe.

01:03:06.173 --> 01:03:09.133
lt is as we feared, Minerva.

01:03:09.383 --> 01:03:13.923
The Chamber of Secrets
has indeed been opened again.

01:03:16.763 --> 01:03:20.893
Again? You mean the Chamber
of Secrets has been opened before?

01:03:21.063 --> 01:03:23.813
Of course.
Don't you see?

01:03:23.983 --> 01:03:26.983
Lucius Malfoy must have opened it
when he was at school here.

01:03:27.603 --> 01:03:30.193
-Now he's taught Draco how to do it.
-Maybe.

01:03:30.363 --> 01:03:33.533
We'll have to wait for
the Polyjuice Potion to know for sure.

01:03:33.693 --> 01:03:37.663
Enlighten me. Why are we brewing
this potion in broad daylight. . .

01:03:37.823 --> 01:03:41.793
. . .in the middle of the girls' lavatory?
Don't you think we'll get caught?

01:03:42.663 --> 01:03:45.333
No. No one ever comes in here.

01:03:46.173 --> 01:03:48.713
-Why?
-Moaning Myrtle.

01:03:48.883 --> 01:03:50.843
Who?

01:03:51.343 --> 01:03:53.013
Moaning Myrtle.

01:03:53.303 --> 01:03:56.633
-Who's Moaning Myrtle?
-l'm Moaning Myrtle.

01:04:02.563 --> 01:04:04.933
l wouldn't expect you to know me.

01:04:05.103 --> 01:04:08.153
Who would ever talk
about ugly, miserable. . .

01:04:08.313 --> 01:04:11.693
. . .moping Moaning Myrtle?

01:04:18.913 --> 01:04:21.033
She's a little sensitive.

01:04:25.543 --> 01:04:27.503
Gather round!

01:04:27.833 --> 01:04:32.843
Gather round.
Can everybody see me?

01:04:33.003 --> 01:04:36.133
Can you all hear me?

01:04:36.803 --> 01:04:38.133
Excellent.

01:04:38.633 --> 01:04:42.353
ln light of the dark events
of recent weeks. . .

01:04:42.513 --> 01:04:47.183
. . .Professor Dumbledore has granted me
permission to start this Dueling Club. . .

01:04:47.353 --> 01:04:52.023
. . .to train you all up in case
you ever need to defend yourselves. . .

01:04:52.273 --> 01:04:54.823
. . .as l myself have done
on countless occasions.

01:04:55.033 --> 01:04:58.703
For full details,
see my published works.

01:05:03.413 --> 01:05:06.543
Let me introduce my assistant. . .

01:05:06.703 --> 01:05:09.333
. . .Professor Snape.

01:05:12.673 --> 01:05:15.463
He has sportingly agreed to help
with a short demonstration.

01:05:15.633 --> 01:05:17.673
l don't want any of you
youngsters to worry.

01:05:17.843 --> 01:05:22.763
You'll still have your Potions master
when l'm through with him. Never fear.

01:05:38.403 --> 01:05:40.033
One.

01:05:40.203 --> 01:05:41.243
Two.

01:05:42.033 --> 01:05:45.083
-Three!
-Expelliarmus!

01:05:53.673 --> 01:05:56.343
-Do you think he's all right?
-Who cares?

01:05:56.503 --> 01:05:59.473
An excellent idea to show them that,
Professor Snape. . .

01:05:59.633 --> 01:06:04.183
. . .but if you don't mind me saying, it was
obvious what you were about to do.

01:06:04.353 --> 01:06:07.603
lf l had wanted to stop you,
it would have been only too easy.

01:06:07.773 --> 01:06:11.233
Perhaps it would be prudent
to first teach the students. . .

01:06:11.393 --> 01:06:15.903
. . .to block unfriendly spells,
professor.

01:06:17.653 --> 01:06:20.073
An excellent suggestion,
Professor Snape.

01:06:21.323 --> 01:06:25.573
Let's have a volunteer pair.
Potter, Weasley, how about you?

01:06:25.743 --> 01:06:29.243
Weasley's wand causes devastation
with the simplest spells.

01:06:29.663 --> 01:06:33.373
We'll be sending Potter
to the hospital wing in a matchbox.

01:06:33.543 --> 01:06:37.633
Might l suggest someone
from my own house?

01:06:38.883 --> 01:06:41.383
Malfoy, perhaps?

01:06:48.893 --> 01:06:51.393
-Good luck, Potter.
-Thank you, sir.

01:06:59.363 --> 01:07:01.363
Wands at the ready.

01:07:01.943 --> 01:07:04.953
-Scared, Potter?
-You wish.

01:07:15.373 --> 01:07:17.083
On the count of three. . .

01:07:17.253 --> 01:07:21.593
. . .cast your charms to disarm
your opponent. Only to disarm.

01:07:21.763 --> 01:07:25.303
We don't want any accidents here.
One.

01:07:27.093 --> 01:07:29.643
-Two.
-Everte Statum!

01:07:41.283 --> 01:07:43.533
Rictusempra!

01:07:54.503 --> 01:07:56.293
l said disarm only.

01:07:56.463 --> 01:07:58.463
Serpensortia!

01:08:07.133 --> 01:08:09.933
Don't move, Potter.
l'll get rid of it for you.

01:08:10.103 --> 01:08:15.523
Allow me, Professor Snape.
Alarte Ascendare!

01:08:58.063 --> 01:09:00.733
Vipera Evanesca.

01:09:07.443 --> 01:09:09.823
What are you playing at?

01:09:22.583 --> 01:09:25.303
You're a Parselmouth?
Why didn't you tell us?

01:09:25.463 --> 01:09:27.723
-l'm a what?
-You can talk to snakes.

01:09:27.883 --> 01:09:33.223
l know. l accidentally set a python
on my cousin Dudley at the zoo once.

01:09:33.393 --> 01:09:37.353
Once. But so what?
l bet loads of people here can do it.

01:09:37.523 --> 01:09:41.273
No, they can't.
lt's not a very common gift, Harry.

01:09:41.773 --> 01:09:43.483
This is bad.

01:09:43.653 --> 01:09:47.403
What's bad? lf l hadn't told
that snake not to attack Justin--

01:09:47.573 --> 01:09:51.033
-That's what you said to it.
-You were there. You heard me.

01:09:51.203 --> 01:09:55.083
l heard you speaking Parseltongue.
Snake language.

01:09:55.243 --> 01:09:58.123
l spoke a different language?

01:09:59.203 --> 01:10:01.583
But l didn't realize--

01:10:01.753 --> 01:10:04.543
How can l speak a language
without knowing l can?

01:10:04.713 --> 01:10:08.713
l don't know, but it sounded like you
were egging the snake on or something.

01:10:08.883 --> 01:10:10.593
Harry, listen to me.

01:10:11.013 --> 01:10:13.893
There's a reason the symbol
of Slytherin house is a serpent.

01:10:14.053 --> 01:10:18.563
Salazar Slytherin was a Parselmouth.
He could talk to snakes too.

01:10:18.813 --> 01:10:19.853
Exactly.

01:10:20.023 --> 01:10:23.403
Now the whole school's gonna think
you're his great-great-great grandson.

01:10:23.563 --> 01:10:25.563
But l'm not.

01:10:28.283 --> 01:10:30.243
l can't be.

01:10:31.363 --> 01:10:33.413
He lived a thousand years ago.

01:10:33.573 --> 01:10:36.783
For all we know, you could be.

01:11:06.903 --> 01:11:09.273
l'll see you back in the common room.

01:11:25.673 --> 01:11:29.963
I want blood.

01:11:32.843 --> 01:11:37.853
They all must die.

01:11:38.433 --> 01:11:40.433
Kill.

01:11:41.103 --> 01:11:43.183
Kill.

01:11:43.983 --> 01:11:46.273
Kill.

01:11:46.603 --> 01:11:50.653
Time to kill.

01:12:24.853 --> 01:12:26.773
Caught in the act.

01:12:26.943 --> 01:12:28.903
l'll have you out this time, Potter.

01:12:29.403 --> 01:12:31.903
Mark my words.

01:12:32.073 --> 01:12:36.323
No. Mr. Filch! You don't understand--

01:13:03.063 --> 01:13:05.023
Professor. . .

01:13:05.183 --> 01:13:06.563
. . .l swear l didn't.

01:13:06.773 --> 01:13:09.983
This is out of my hands, Potter.

01:13:19.613 --> 01:13:22.283
Professor Dumbledore
will be waiting for you.

01:13:31.213 --> 01:13:33.793
Sherbet Lemon.

01:14:07.753 --> 01:14:09.873
Professor Dumbledore?

01:14:26.353 --> 01:14:29.063
Bee in your bonnet, Potter?

01:14:31.943 --> 01:14:36.483
l was just wondering
if you put me in the right house.

01:14:36.653 --> 01:14:42.113
Yes. You were particularly
difficult to place.

01:14:42.283 --> 01:14:45.823
But l stand by what l said last year.

01:14:45.993 --> 01:14:49.373
You would have done well in Slytherin.

01:14:49.543 --> 01:14:50.873
You're wrong.

01:15:20.153 --> 01:15:21.573
Harry?

01:15:21.943 --> 01:15:24.203
Professor.

01:15:24.363 --> 01:15:28.163
Your bird. . . .
There was nothing l could do.

01:15:28.743 --> 01:15:32.083
-He just caught fire.
-And about time too.

01:15:32.913 --> 01:15:35.253
He's been looking dreadful for days.

01:15:35.423 --> 01:15:37.423
Pity you had to see him
on a burning day.

01:15:39.343 --> 01:15:42.593
Fawkes is a phoenix, Harry.

01:15:42.763 --> 01:15:46.093
They burst into flame
when it is time for them to die. . .

01:15:46.263 --> 01:15:48.393
. . .and then they are. . .

01:15:48.553 --> 01:15:51.603
. . .reborn from the ashes.

01:15:59.983 --> 01:16:02.613
Fascinating creatures, phoenixes.

01:16:03.073 --> 01:16:06.953
They can carry immensely heavy loads.

01:16:07.113 --> 01:16:09.953
Their tears have healing powers.

01:16:12.583 --> 01:16:15.623
Professor Dumbledore, sir!
Wait! Listen!

01:16:16.623 --> 01:16:18.753
Professor Dumbledore, sir,
it wasn't Harry.

01:16:19.923 --> 01:16:22.803
l'd be prepared to swear it
in front of the Ministry of Magic.

01:16:24.263 --> 01:16:26.133
Relax.

01:16:26.883 --> 01:16:28.843
l do not believe. . .

01:16:29.013 --> 01:16:32.513
-. . .that Harry attacked anyone.
-Of course you don't.

01:16:36.273 --> 01:16:38.853
Right. Well, l'll. . . .

01:16:39.023 --> 01:16:42.153
-l'll just wait outside, then.
-Yes.

01:16:45.823 --> 01:16:49.493
-You don't think it was me, professor?
-No, Harry.

01:16:49.663 --> 01:16:52.163
l do not think it was you.

01:16:53.203 --> 01:16:55.003
But l must ask you. . .

01:16:55.583 --> 01:16:59.673
. . .is there something
you wish to tell me?

01:17:06.133 --> 01:17:08.053
No, sir.

01:17:08.223 --> 01:17:09.723
Nothing.

01:17:12.723 --> 01:17:14.893
Very well, then.

01:17:15.063 --> 01:17:16.853
Off you go.

01:17:54.813 --> 01:17:58.353
Everything's set. We just need a bit
of who you're changing into.

01:17:58.523 --> 01:18:00.233
Crabbe and Goyle.

01:18:00.393 --> 01:18:03.193
We also need to make sure
that the real Crabbe and Goyle. . .

01:18:03.363 --> 01:18:06.573
. . .can't burst in on us
while we're interrogating Malfoy.

01:18:06.903 --> 01:18:09.613
-How?
-l've got it all worked out.

01:18:09.783 --> 01:18:12.363
l filled these
with a simple Sleeping Draught.

01:18:12.533 --> 01:18:15.283
Simple, but powerful.

01:18:15.493 --> 01:18:17.663
Now, once they're asleep. . .

01:18:17.833 --> 01:18:21.043
. . .hide them in the broomstick cupboard
and pull out a few of their hairs. . .

01:18:21.213 --> 01:18:23.083
. . .and put on their uniforms.

01:18:23.253 --> 01:18:26.553
-Whose hair are you ripping out, then?
-l've already got mine.

01:18:26.713 --> 01:18:29.883
Millicent Bulstrode. Slytherin.

01:18:30.053 --> 01:18:32.223
l got this off her robes.

01:18:32.383 --> 01:18:35.013
l'm going to go check
on the Polyjuice Potion.

01:18:35.183 --> 01:18:37.893
Make sure that Crabbe and Goyle
find these.

01:18:50.033 --> 01:18:52.403
Ron, maybe l should do it.

01:18:52.573 --> 01:18:54.623
Yeah. Right.

01:18:56.833 --> 01:18:58.663
Wingardium Leviosa.

01:19:08.803 --> 01:19:10.423
Cool.

01:19:33.573 --> 01:19:35.413
How thick could you get?

01:19:35.573 --> 01:19:37.533
Come on, let's get them.

01:19:40.203 --> 01:19:44.213
We'll have exactly one hour
before we change back into ourselves.

01:19:52.383 --> 01:19:54.343
Add the hairs.

01:19:58.893 --> 01:20:00.643
Essence of Crabbe.

01:20:00.813 --> 01:20:02.683
Cheers.

01:20:11.403 --> 01:20:13.823
l think l'm gonna be sick.

01:20:16.743 --> 01:20:18.573
Me too.

01:21:03.453 --> 01:21:05.203
Harry?

01:21:05.663 --> 01:21:07.213
Ron.

01:21:07.963 --> 01:21:10.133
Bloody hell!

01:21:10.923 --> 01:21:13.213
We still sound like ourselves.

01:21:13.383 --> 01:21:15.133
You need to sound more like Crabbe.

01:21:16.303 --> 01:21:18.593
-Bloody hell.
-Excellent.

01:21:18.933 --> 01:21:21.433
-But where's Hermione?
-l. . . .

01:21:21.603 --> 01:21:24.603
l don't think l'm going.
You go on without me.

01:21:24.773 --> 01:21:26.483
Hermione, are you okay?

01:21:26.643 --> 01:21:29.483
Just go. You're wasting time.

01:21:31.563 --> 01:21:33.233
Come on.

01:21:36.743 --> 01:21:40.073
l think the Slytherin common room's
this way.

01:21:43.083 --> 01:21:45.543
Excuse me.

01:21:47.333 --> 01:21:49.253
What are you doing d--?

01:21:49.423 --> 01:21:51.503
l mean, what are you doing down here?

01:21:53.423 --> 01:21:56.133
l happen to be a school prefect.

01:21:56.303 --> 01:22:00.763
You, on the other hand, have no business
wandering the corridors at night.

01:22:01.343 --> 01:22:03.183
What are your names again?

01:22:03.353 --> 01:22:07.353
-l'm. . . .
-Crabbe, Goyle, where have you been?

01:22:07.523 --> 01:22:10.563
Pigging out in the Great Hall
all this time?

01:22:12.063 --> 01:22:14.363
Why are you wearing glasses?

01:22:15.193 --> 01:22:18.033
-Reading.
-Reading?

01:22:19.193 --> 01:22:21.493
l didn't know you could read.

01:22:24.373 --> 01:22:26.453
And what are you doing down here,
Weasley?

01:22:26.623 --> 01:22:28.663
Mind your attitude, Malfoy.

01:22:37.463 --> 01:22:39.473
Well, sit down.

01:22:42.263 --> 01:22:46.103
You'd never know the Weasleys
were pure-bloods, the way they behave.

01:22:46.313 --> 01:22:50.143
They're an embarrassment
to the wizarding world. All of them.

01:22:50.983 --> 01:22:53.273
What's wrong with you, Crabbe?

01:22:55.483 --> 01:22:57.233
Stomachache.

01:22:59.233 --> 01:23:04.073
l'm surprised the Daily Prophet
hasn't done a report on all these attacks.

01:23:04.243 --> 01:23:06.703
l suppose Dumbledore
is trying to hush it all up.

01:23:06.993 --> 01:23:09.373
Father always said Dumbledore
was the worst thing. . .

01:23:09.543 --> 01:23:13.333
-. . .that ever happened to this place.
-You're wrong!

01:23:20.843 --> 01:23:22.013
What?

01:23:22.173 --> 01:23:25.843
You think there's someone here
who's worse than Dumbledore?

01:23:26.013 --> 01:23:28.433
Well? Do you?

01:23:28.973 --> 01:23:30.853
Harry Potter?

01:23:37.403 --> 01:23:38.823
Good one, Goyle.

01:23:38.983 --> 01:23:40.533
You're absolutely right.

01:23:41.193 --> 01:23:43.033
Saint Potter.

01:23:44.033 --> 01:23:46.823
And people actually think
that he's the Heir of Slytherin?

01:23:50.583 --> 01:23:53.213
But then you must have some idea
who's behind it all.

01:23:53.373 --> 01:23:57.043
You know l don't, Goyle.
l told you yesterday.

01:23:58.043 --> 01:24:00.553
How many times do l have to tell you?

01:24:01.553 --> 01:24:03.383
ls this yours?

01:24:07.853 --> 01:24:10.223
But my father did say this:

01:24:10.603 --> 01:24:13.523
lt's been 50 years
since the Chamber was opened.

01:24:13.683 --> 01:24:18.063
He wouldn't tell me who opened it.
Only that they were expelled.

01:24:18.363 --> 01:24:23.033
The last time the Chamber of Secrets
was opened, a Mudblood died.

01:24:23.193 --> 01:24:27.493
So it's only a matter of time
before one of them is killed this time.

01:24:28.073 --> 01:24:29.913
As for me. . .

01:24:30.083 --> 01:24:32.243
. . .l hope it's Granger.

01:24:32.413 --> 01:24:34.623
What's the matter with you two?

01:24:34.793 --> 01:24:37.293
You're acting very odd.

01:24:37.463 --> 01:24:39.673
lt's his stomachache.

01:24:39.843 --> 01:24:41.923
Calm down.

01:24:46.093 --> 01:24:48.093
Scar.

01:24:51.683 --> 01:24:53.103
Hair.

01:24:59.273 --> 01:25:01.653
Hey! Where are you going?

01:25:04.653 --> 01:25:05.943
That was close.

01:25:06.113 --> 01:25:08.533
Hermione, come out.
We've got loads to tell you.

01:25:08.703 --> 01:25:10.573
Go away.

01:25:11.083 --> 01:25:14.953
Wait till you see. lt's awful.

01:25:16.913 --> 01:25:18.673
Hermione?

01:25:18.833 --> 01:25:20.463
Are you okay?

01:25:22.503 --> 01:25:24.303
Do you remember me telling you. . .

01:25:24.463 --> 01:25:27.633
. . .that the Polyjuice Potion
was only for human transformations?

01:25:27.803 --> 01:25:31.933
lt was cat hair l plucked off
Millicent Bulstrode's robes.

01:25:34.313 --> 01:25:35.853
Look at my face.

01:25:36.983 --> 01:25:39.443
Look at your tail.

01:25:45.993 --> 01:25:47.443
Have you spoken to Hermione?

01:25:47.613 --> 01:25:50.163
She should be out of hospital
in a few days. . .

01:25:50.323 --> 01:25:53.163
. . .when she stops coughing up fur balls.

01:25:57.913 --> 01:25:59.673
What's this?

01:26:04.253 --> 01:26:05.343
Yuck!

01:26:05.503 --> 01:26:08.303
Looks like Moaning Myrtle's
flooded the bathroom.

01:26:24.523 --> 01:26:28.653
-Come to throw something else at me?
-Why would l throw something at you?

01:26:29.073 --> 01:26:33.163
Don't ask me. Here l am,
minding my own business. . .

01:26:33.323 --> 01:26:36.953
. . .and someone thinks it's funny
to throw a book at me.

01:26:37.163 --> 01:26:40.043
But it can't hurt if someone
throws something at you.

01:26:40.213 --> 01:26:42.623
l mean, it'll just go
right through you.

01:26:43.673 --> 01:26:48.053
Sure! Let's all throw books at Myrtle
because she can't feel it.

01:26:48.213 --> 01:26:50.843
Ten points
if you get it through her stomach!

01:26:51.013 --> 01:26:54.513
Fifty points if it goes through her head!

01:26:55.013 --> 01:26:59.433
-But who threw it at you, anyway?
-l don't know. l didn't see them.

01:26:59.773 --> 01:27:04.023
l was just sitting in the U-bend,
thinking about death. . .

01:27:04.233 --> 01:27:07.903
. . .and it fell through the top
of my head.

01:27:38.063 --> 01:27:40.563
''Tom Marvolo Riddle. ''

01:28:10.423 --> 01:28:12.763
My name. . .

01:28:12.923 --> 01:28:15.843
. . .is Harry. . .

01:28:17.473 --> 01:28:19.603
. . .Potter.

01:28:32.823 --> 01:28:37.993
Do you know anything. . .

01:28:38.823 --> 01:28:45.503
. . .about the Chamber of Secrets?

01:28:55.633 --> 01:28:57.553
Can you. . .

01:28:58.803 --> 01:29:01.103
. . .tell me?

01:30:03.373 --> 01:30:06.793
Excuse me. Could you tell me
what's going on here?

01:30:10.253 --> 01:30:12.583
Are you Tom Riddle?

01:30:12.753 --> 01:30:14.553
Hello, can you hear me?

01:30:35.113 --> 01:30:36.863
Riddle!

01:30:37.443 --> 01:30:38.993
Come.

01:30:39.153 --> 01:30:41.163
Professor Dumbledore.

01:30:43.323 --> 01:30:45.493
Dumbledore?

01:30:46.793 --> 01:30:50.293
lt is not wise to be wandering around
this late hour, Tom.

01:30:50.463 --> 01:30:53.793
Yes, professor. l suppose l. . . .

01:30:53.963 --> 01:30:56.133
l had to see for myself
if the rumors were true.

01:30:56.713 --> 01:30:59.633
l'm afraid they are, Tom.
They are true.

01:30:59.803 --> 01:31:02.643
About the school as well?
l don't have a home to go to.

01:31:02.803 --> 01:31:05.643
They wouldn't really close Hogwarts,
would they, professor?

01:31:05.803 --> 01:31:08.353
l understand, Tom, but l'm afraid. . .

01:31:09.143 --> 01:31:12.063
. . .Headmaster Dippet
may have no choice.

01:31:12.233 --> 01:31:16.733
Sir, if it all stopped,
if the person responsible was caught. . . .

01:31:18.983 --> 01:31:21.113
ls there something. . .

01:31:22.033 --> 01:31:24.033
. . .you wish to tell me?

01:31:25.243 --> 01:31:27.793
No, sir. Nothing.

01:31:34.543 --> 01:31:37.593
Very well, then. Off you go.

01:31:37.753 --> 01:31:39.633
Good night, sir.

01:32:15.753 --> 01:32:18.673
-Let's get you out of there.
-Evening, Hagrid.

01:32:19.003 --> 01:32:23.343
l'm going to have to turn you in. l don't
think you meant it to kill anyone. . . .

01:32:23.513 --> 01:32:25.803
You can't. You don't understand.

01:32:26.013 --> 01:32:29.143
The dead girl's parents will be here
tomorrow. The least Hogwarts can do. . .

01:32:29.313 --> 01:32:32.223
. . .is make sure the thing that killed
their daughter is slaughtered.

01:32:32.473 --> 01:32:35.603
lt wasn't him.
Aragog never killed no one. Never.

01:32:35.943 --> 01:32:38.113
Monsters don't make good pets, Hagrid.

01:32:38.273 --> 01:32:39.903
-Now, stand aside.
-No!

01:32:40.073 --> 01:32:42.033
-Stand aside, Hagrid.
-No!

01:32:42.193 --> 01:32:43.823
Cistem Aperio!

01:32:50.783 --> 01:32:53.123
Arania Exumai!

01:32:54.003 --> 01:32:55.463
Aragog!

01:32:55.623 --> 01:32:56.873
Aragog!

01:32:57.423 --> 01:32:58.793
l can't let you go.

01:32:59.343 --> 01:33:02.633
They'll have your wand for this, Hagrid.
You'll be expelled.

01:33:05.173 --> 01:33:07.053
Hagrid!

01:33:37.083 --> 01:33:41.213
lt was Hagrid. Hagrid opened
the Chamber of Secrets 50 years ago.

01:33:41.383 --> 01:33:44.343
lt can't be Hagrid.
lt just can't be.

01:33:44.513 --> 01:33:48.593
We don't even know this Tom Riddle.
He sounds like a dirty, rotten snitch.

01:33:48.763 --> 01:33:52.263
The monster had killed somebody, Ron.
What would any of us have done?

01:33:52.553 --> 01:33:56.523
Look, Hagrid's our friend. Why don't
we just go and ask him about it?

01:33:56.733 --> 01:33:59.403
That would be a cheerful visit.
''Hello, Hagrid.

01:33:59.563 --> 01:34:03.403
Tell us, have you been setting anything
mad and hairy loose in the castle lately?''

01:34:03.573 --> 01:34:06.783
Mad and hairy? You wouldn't be talking
about me, now, would you?

01:34:07.073 --> 01:34:08.113
No.

01:34:12.623 --> 01:34:14.243
What's that you've got, Hagrid?

01:34:14.703 --> 01:34:19.253
lt's Flesh-Eating Slug Repellent.
For the Mandrakes, you know.

01:34:19.423 --> 01:34:23.093
Now, according to Professor Sprout,
they've still got a bit of growing to do.

01:34:23.253 --> 01:34:26.763
But once their acne's cleared up,
we'll chop them up and stew them. . .

01:34:26.923 --> 01:34:30.223
. . .and then we'll get those people
down at the hospital un-Petrified.

01:34:31.683 --> 01:34:34.563
ln the meantime, though, you three. . .

01:34:34.723 --> 01:34:37.893
. . .had best be looking after yourselves.
All right?

01:34:45.773 --> 01:34:47.693
Hello, Neville.

01:34:48.783 --> 01:34:51.283
Harry, l don't know who did it,
but you'd better come.

01:34:51.663 --> 01:34:53.373
Come on!

01:35:15.933 --> 01:35:19.933
lt had to be a Gryffindor.
Nobody else knows our password.

01:35:20.103 --> 01:35:22.353
Unless it wasn't a student.

01:35:22.523 --> 01:35:25.943
Whoever it was, they must have
been looking for something.

01:35:26.113 --> 01:35:27.523
And they found it.

01:35:28.283 --> 01:35:30.783
Tom Riddle's diary is gone.

01:35:32.363 --> 01:35:33.663
All right, listen up.

01:35:33.823 --> 01:35:36.743
We play our game,
Hufflepuff doesn't stand a chance.

01:35:36.913 --> 01:35:38.793
We're stronger, quicker and smarter.

01:35:38.953 --> 01:35:41.963
Not to mention they're dead scared
that Harry will Petrify them. . .

01:35:42.123 --> 01:35:45.633
-. . .if they fly anywhere near him.
-Well, that too.

01:35:46.843 --> 01:35:48.383
Professor McGonagall.

01:35:48.553 --> 01:35:51.593
-This match has been canceled.
-We can't cancel Quidditch.

01:35:51.763 --> 01:35:56.723
Silence, Wood. You and your teammates
will go to Gryffindor Tower. Now.

01:35:56.893 --> 01:35:59.563
Potter, you and l will find Mr. Weasley.

01:35:59.933 --> 01:36:02.483
There's something
the both of you have to see.

01:36:04.563 --> 01:36:08.153
l warn you.
This could be a wee bit of a shock.

01:36:16.533 --> 01:36:17.743
Hermione!

01:36:17.913 --> 01:36:19.703
She was found near the library. . .

01:36:20.953 --> 01:36:23.003
. . .along with this.

01:36:24.463 --> 01:36:27.293
Does it mean anything to either of you?

01:36:27.463 --> 01:36:28.923
No.

01:36:43.143 --> 01:36:45.483
Could l have your attention, please?

01:36:45.643 --> 01:36:51.283
Because of recent events, these new
rules will be put into effect immediately:

01:36:51.613 --> 01:36:56.743
''All students will return to their house
common rooms by 6:00 every evening.

01:36:56.913 --> 01:37:00.993
All students will be escorted
to each lesson by a teacher.

01:37:01.163 --> 01:37:04.163
No exceptions. ''

01:37:04.833 --> 01:37:06.873
l should tell you this:

01:37:07.043 --> 01:37:11.173
Unless the culprit
behind these attacks is caught. . .

01:37:11.713 --> 01:37:14.883
. . .it is likely the school will be closed.

01:37:26.393 --> 01:37:29.363
We've got to talk to Hagrid, Ron.
l can't believe it's him. . .

01:37:29.523 --> 01:37:31.823
. . .but if he did set the monster loose
last time. . .

01:37:31.983 --> 01:37:35.153
. . .he'll know how to get inside
the Chamber of Secrets. That's a start.

01:37:35.323 --> 01:37:36.573
But you heard McGonagall.

01:37:36.743 --> 01:37:40.033
We're not allowed to leave
the tower except for class.

01:37:40.493 --> 01:37:42.953
l think it's time to get
my dad's old cloak out again.

01:37:56.593 --> 01:37:58.303
Who's there?

01:38:02.103 --> 01:38:03.683
Hello?

01:38:04.313 --> 01:38:05.853
Hello?

01:38:07.023 --> 01:38:11.313
-What's that for?
-Nothing. l was expecting. . . .

01:38:11.483 --> 01:38:15.363
lt doesn't matter. Come on in.
l just made a pot of tea.

01:38:18.113 --> 01:38:20.413
Hagrid, are you okay?

01:38:20.573 --> 01:38:23.453
l'm fine. l'm all right.

01:38:24.413 --> 01:38:26.123
Did you hear about Hermione?

01:38:26.623 --> 01:38:30.293
Yeah. l heard about that, all right.

01:38:30.623 --> 01:38:34.293
Look, we have to ask you something.

01:38:35.963 --> 01:38:39.473
Do you know who's opened
the Chamber of Secrets?

01:38:41.803 --> 01:38:44.103
What you had to understand
about that is--

01:38:45.763 --> 01:38:47.353
Quick, under the cloak.

01:38:48.023 --> 01:38:51.103
Don't say a word.
Be quiet, both of you.

01:38:57.533 --> 01:39:00.613
-Professor Dumbledore, sir.
-Good evening, Hagrid.

01:39:00.783 --> 01:39:03.203
l wonder, could we. . .?

01:39:03.373 --> 01:39:05.873
Of course. Come in. Come in.

01:39:06.043 --> 01:39:07.413
That's Dad's boss.

01:39:07.583 --> 01:39:11.173
Cornelius Fudge, Minister of Magic.

01:39:11.333 --> 01:39:15.713
Bad business, Hagrid, very bad business.
Had to come.

01:39:15.883 --> 01:39:19.133
Three attacks on Muggle-borns.
Things have gone far enough.

01:39:19.303 --> 01:39:22.513
-The Ministry's got to act.
-But l never--

01:39:22.723 --> 01:39:24.513
You know l never, professor.

01:39:24.683 --> 01:39:27.773
l want it understood, Cornelius. . .

01:39:27.933 --> 01:39:29.773
. . .that Hagrid. . .

01:39:29.933 --> 01:39:32.233
. . .has my full confidence.

01:39:32.393 --> 01:39:36.193
Albus, look,
Hagrid's record is against him.

01:39:36.363 --> 01:39:38.903
-l've got to take him.
-Take me?

01:39:39.073 --> 01:39:41.363
Take me where?
Not Azkaban prison.

01:39:41.653 --> 01:39:45.413
l'm afraid we have no choice, Hagrid.

01:39:46.033 --> 01:39:47.953
Already here, Fudge?

01:39:48.123 --> 01:39:49.453
Good.

01:39:50.373 --> 01:39:53.123
What are you doing here?
Get out of my house!

01:39:53.793 --> 01:39:55.333
Believe me. . .

01:39:55.633 --> 01:39:59.843
. . .l take absolutely no pleasure
being inside your. . . .

01:40:01.723 --> 01:40:03.933
You call this a house?

01:40:05.013 --> 01:40:06.053
No.

01:40:06.223 --> 01:40:10.103
l simply called up the school
and was told the headmaster was here.

01:40:10.273 --> 01:40:14.353
Well, what exactly is it
that you want with me?

01:40:14.903 --> 01:40:19.653
The other governors and l have decided
it's time for you to step aside.

01:40:21.283 --> 01:40:24.203
This is an order of suspension.

01:40:29.743 --> 01:40:33.123
You'll find all 1 2 signatures on it.

01:40:37.003 --> 01:40:41.213
l'm afraid we feel
you've rather lost your touch.

01:40:41.923 --> 01:40:44.263
Well, what, with all these attacks. . .

01:40:44.433 --> 01:40:47.223
. . .there'll be no
Muggle-borns left at Hogwarts.

01:40:47.393 --> 01:40:51.933
l can only imagine what an awful loss
that would be to the school.

01:40:52.103 --> 01:40:54.313
You can't take
Professor Dumbledore away.

01:40:54.603 --> 01:40:57.153
Take him away and the Muggle-borns
won't stand a chance.

01:40:57.313 --> 01:40:59.773
You mark my words,
there'll be killings next!

01:40:59.943 --> 01:41:01.613
You think so?

01:41:01.783 --> 01:41:04.283
Calm yourself, Hagrid.

01:41:05.613 --> 01:41:08.373
lf the governors desire my removal. . .

01:41:08.533 --> 01:41:12.243
. . .l will, of course, step aside.

01:41:13.833 --> 01:41:16.083
However. . .

01:41:16.753 --> 01:41:21.303
. . .you will find that help
will always be given at Hogwarts. . .

01:41:21.463 --> 01:41:23.343
. . .to those who. . .

01:41:23.513 --> 01:41:25.843
. . .ask for it.

01:41:32.643 --> 01:41:34.983
Admirable sentiments.

01:41:35.143 --> 01:41:36.983
Shall we?

01:41:49.073 --> 01:41:50.623
Fudge.

01:41:52.333 --> 01:41:54.163
Come, Hagrid.

01:41:55.293 --> 01:41:56.833
Well?

01:41:57.503 --> 01:41:58.583
lf. . . .

01:41:59.003 --> 01:42:01.543
lf anybody was looking for some stuff. . .

01:42:01.713 --> 01:42:06.593
. . .then all they'd have to do
would be to follow the spiders.

01:42:06.763 --> 01:42:09.343
Yep. That would lead them right.

01:42:09.513 --> 01:42:11.473
That's all l have to say.

01:42:13.183 --> 01:42:16.933
And someone will need
to feed Fang while l'm away.

01:42:20.313 --> 01:42:22.313
Good boy.

01:42:28.453 --> 01:42:30.573
Hagrid's right.

01:42:30.743 --> 01:42:33.703
With Dumbledore gone,
there'll be an attack a day.

01:42:33.873 --> 01:42:35.543
Look.

01:42:41.583 --> 01:42:43.383
Come on.

01:42:47.093 --> 01:42:49.133
Come on, Fang.

01:43:07.403 --> 01:43:08.783
Come on.

01:43:08.943 --> 01:43:10.243
What?

01:43:10.403 --> 01:43:13.663
You heard what Hagrid said.
''Follow the spiders. ''

01:43:13.873 --> 01:43:16.493
They're heading to the Dark Forest.

01:43:18.543 --> 01:43:23.003
Why spiders? Why couldn't it be
''follow the butterflies''?

01:43:58.743 --> 01:44:01.503
Harry, l don't like this.

01:44:06.633 --> 01:44:09.843
-Harry, l don't like this at all.
-Shush!

01:44:21.353 --> 01:44:23.893
Can we go back now?

01:44:24.063 --> 01:44:25.813
Come on.

01:45:15.533 --> 01:45:18.283
Who is it?

01:45:18.953 --> 01:45:20.083
Don't panic.

01:45:20.413 --> 01:45:21.913
Hagrid?

01:45:22.333 --> 01:45:23.913
ls that you?

01:45:24.503 --> 01:45:26.423
We're friends of Hagrid's.

01:45:44.523 --> 01:45:47.733
And you?
You're Aragog, aren't you?

01:45:48.353 --> 01:45:49.653
Yes.

01:45:49.813 --> 01:45:53.613
Hagrid has never sent
men into our hollow before.

01:45:53.783 --> 01:45:56.903
He's in trouble. Up at the school,
there have been attacks.

01:45:57.533 --> 01:45:59.373
They think it's Hagrid.

01:45:59.533 --> 01:46:03.163
They think he opened
the Chamber of Secrets. Like before.

01:46:03.373 --> 01:46:05.703
That's a lie.

01:46:06.163 --> 01:46:09.083
Hagrid never opened
the Chamber of Secrets.

01:46:09.713 --> 01:46:12.593
-Then you're not the monster?
-No.

01:46:12.753 --> 01:46:15.803
The monster was born in the castle.

01:46:16.013 --> 01:46:21.303
l came to Hagrid from a distant land
in the pocket of a traveler.

01:46:21.933 --> 01:46:23.563
Harry.

01:46:25.473 --> 01:46:30.063
But if you're not the monster, then
what did kill that girl 50 years ago?

01:46:30.233 --> 01:46:33.233
We do not speak of it.

01:46:33.573 --> 01:46:39.113
lt is an ancient creature we
spiders fear above all others.

01:46:39.283 --> 01:46:41.073
But have you seen it?

01:46:41.743 --> 01:46:47.583
l never saw any part of the castle
but the box in which Hagrid kept me.

01:46:47.753 --> 01:46:50.923
The girl was discovered
in a bathroom.

01:46:51.083 --> 01:46:55.593
When l was accused,
Hagrid brought me here.

01:46:55.753 --> 01:46:57.763
-Harry!
-What?

01:47:10.603 --> 01:47:13.613
Well, thank you.

01:47:14.573 --> 01:47:16.733
We'll just go.

01:47:17.193 --> 01:47:18.943
Go?

01:47:19.153 --> 01:47:20.953
l think not.

01:47:21.113 --> 01:47:26.583
My sons and daughters
do not harm Hagrid on my command.

01:47:26.743 --> 01:47:29.163
But l cannot deny them
fresh meat. . .

01:47:29.333 --> 01:47:33.673
. . .when it wanders
so willingly into our midst.

01:47:33.833 --> 01:47:37.633
Goodbye, friend of Hagrid.

01:47:37.803 --> 01:47:39.633
Can we panic now?

01:47:50.353 --> 01:47:52.273
Know any spells?

01:47:52.443 --> 01:47:55.613
One, but it's not powerful
enough for all of them.

01:47:55.773 --> 01:47:58.533
Where's Hermione when you need her?

01:48:12.043 --> 01:48:13.333
Let's go!

01:48:18.463 --> 01:48:20.553
Arania Exumai!

01:48:25.843 --> 01:48:27.183
Go!

01:48:45.163 --> 01:48:47.243
Glad we're out of there.

01:48:54.213 --> 01:48:56.543
Arania Exumai!

01:49:02.263 --> 01:49:06.013
-Thanks for that.
-Don't mention it.

01:49:16.943 --> 01:49:19.113
Get us out of here.

01:49:19.613 --> 01:49:21.283
Now!

01:49:23.363 --> 01:49:27.613
Come on!
Come on, move faster!

01:49:30.283 --> 01:49:31.623
Come on! Go!

01:49:49.143 --> 01:49:51.183
Get us in the air.

01:49:52.263 --> 01:49:53.723
The flying gear's jammed!

01:49:57.813 --> 01:50:01.613
-Come on! Pull!
-l'm trying!

01:50:30.933 --> 01:50:33.853
Follow the spiders.
Follow the spiders.

01:50:34.013 --> 01:50:38.353
lf Hagrid ever gets out of Azkaban,
l'll kill him.

01:50:52.373 --> 01:50:55.583
l mean, what was the point
of sending us in there?

01:50:55.743 --> 01:51:00.373
-What have we found out?
-We know one thing.

01:51:00.543 --> 01:51:03.923
Hagrid never opened
the Chamber of Secrets.

01:51:04.133 --> 01:51:06.133
He was innocent.

01:51:21.603 --> 01:51:24.063
Wish you were here, Hermione.

01:51:24.613 --> 01:51:26.903
We need you.

01:51:27.823 --> 01:51:29.903
Now more than ever.

01:51:46.843 --> 01:51:50.263
-What's that?
-Ron. . . .

01:51:51.093 --> 01:51:55.553
This is why Hermione was in
the library the day she was attacked.

01:51:56.103 --> 01:51:57.353
Come on.

01:51:58.023 --> 01:52:00.983
''Of the many fearsome beasts
that roam our land. . .

01:52:01.143 --> 01:52:05.773
. . .none is more deadly than the basilisk.
Capable of living for hundreds of years. . .

01:52:05.943 --> 01:52:09.743
. . .instant death awaits any who meet
this giant serpent's eye.

01:52:09.903 --> 01:52:12.913
Spiders flee before it. ''
Ron, this is it.

01:52:13.073 --> 01:52:15.873
The monster in the Chamber
of Secrets is a basilisk.

01:52:16.033 --> 01:52:19.953
That's why l can hear it speak.
lt's a snake.

01:52:20.293 --> 01:52:25.583
But if it kills by looking people
in the eye, why is it no one's dead?

01:52:36.223 --> 01:52:39.143
Because no one did look it
in the eye.

01:52:41.103 --> 01:52:43.693
Not directly, at least.

01:52:44.943 --> 01:52:47.153
Colin saw it through his camera.

01:52:47.313 --> 01:52:51.363
Justin-- Justin must have seen the
basilisk through Nearly Headless Nick.

01:52:51.533 --> 01:52:55.533
Nick got the full blast of it.
But he's a ghost, he couldn't die again.

01:52:55.703 --> 01:52:58.833
And Hermione had the mirror.

01:52:58.993 --> 01:53:02.373
l bet you she was using it to look
around corners in case it came along.

01:53:02.543 --> 01:53:03.833
And Mrs. Norris?

01:53:04.003 --> 01:53:07.503
l'm pretty sure she didn't have
a camera or a mirror, Harry.

01:53:09.043 --> 01:53:10.923
The water.

01:53:11.383 --> 01:53:16.973
There was water on the floor that night.
She only saw the basilisk's reflection.

01:53:23.103 --> 01:53:25.023
''Spiders flee before it. ''

01:53:25.193 --> 01:53:28.943
-lt all fits.
-How's a basilisk been getting around?

01:53:29.113 --> 01:53:31.943
A dirty, great snake.
Someone would have seen it.

01:53:32.113 --> 01:53:37.783
-Hermione's answered that too.
-Pipes? lt's using the plumbing.

01:53:37.953 --> 01:53:42.203
Remember what Aragog said
about that girl 50 years ago?

01:53:42.373 --> 01:53:46.623
She died in a bathroom?
What if she never left?

01:53:47.293 --> 01:53:48.633
Moaning Myrtle.

01:53:49.593 --> 01:53:53.633
All students are to return
to their house dormitories at once.

01:53:53.803 --> 01:53:57.223
All teachers to the second-floor
corridor immediately.

01:54:02.223 --> 01:54:08.063
As you can see, the Heir of Slytherin
has left another message.

01:54:08.233 --> 01:54:10.443
Our worst fear has been realized.

01:54:10.613 --> 01:54:15.193
A student has been taken by the monster
into the Chamber itself.

01:54:16.243 --> 01:54:21.913
The students must be sent home.
l'm afraid this is the end of Hogwarts.

01:54:24.293 --> 01:54:26.753
So sorry. Dozed off.
What have l missed?

01:54:26.913 --> 01:54:31.253
A girl has been snatched by the monster,
Lockhart. Your moment has come at last.

01:54:31.423 --> 01:54:34.383
-My moment?
-Weren't you saying just last night. . .

01:54:34.553 --> 01:54:39.093
. . .that you've known all along where the
entrance to the Chamber of Secrets is?

01:54:40.433 --> 01:54:45.933
That's settled. We'll leave you
to deal with the monster, Gilderoy.

01:54:46.103 --> 01:54:51.273
-Your skills, after all, are legend.
-Very well.

01:54:51.443 --> 01:54:54.653
l'll just be in my office getting. . . .

01:54:55.483 --> 01:54:57.443
Getting ready.

01:55:00.363 --> 01:55:03.583
Who is it that the monster's taken,
Minerva?

01:55:03.743 --> 01:55:05.583
Ginny Weasley.

01:55:16.963 --> 01:55:20.053
''Her skeleton will lie
in the Chamber forever. ''

01:55:24.103 --> 01:55:25.893
Ginny.

01:55:27.983 --> 01:55:31.483
Lockhart may be useless, but he's
going to try and get into the Chamber.

01:55:31.653 --> 01:55:34.363
At least we can tell him
what we know.

01:55:35.693 --> 01:55:38.283
Professor, we have some information
for you.

01:55:40.033 --> 01:55:41.993
Are you going somewhere?

01:55:42.163 --> 01:55:45.283
Well, yes. Urgent call. Unavoidable.
Got to go.

01:55:45.453 --> 01:55:48.663
-What about my sister?
-Well. . . .

01:55:49.003 --> 01:55:52.503
As to that, most unfortunate.
No one regrets more than l.

01:55:52.673 --> 01:55:56.673
You're the Defense Against the Dark
Arts teacher. You can't go now.

01:55:56.843 --> 01:55:59.843
l must say, when l took the job,
there was nothing in the description--

01:56:00.013 --> 01:56:01.183
You're running away?

01:56:01.343 --> 01:56:04.143
-After all you did in your books?
-Books can be misleading.

01:56:04.303 --> 01:56:06.853
-You wrote them.
-My dear boy, use your common sense.

01:56:07.013 --> 01:56:11.443
My books wouldn't have sold as well if
people didn't think l'd done those things.

01:56:12.023 --> 01:56:13.603
You're a fraud.

01:56:13.773 --> 01:56:16.573
You've been taking credit
for what other wizards have done.

01:56:16.733 --> 01:56:18.693
ls there anything you can do?

01:56:18.863 --> 01:56:23.573
Yes, now you mention it.
l'm rather gifted with Memory Charms.

01:56:23.743 --> 01:56:26.243
Otherwise, all those wizards
would have gone blabbing.

01:56:26.413 --> 01:56:29.543
l'd never have sold another book.

01:56:29.703 --> 01:56:35.423
ln fact, l'm going to have to do
the same to you.

01:56:35.923 --> 01:56:38.713
Don't even think about it.

01:56:49.563 --> 01:56:51.023
Who's there?

01:56:53.443 --> 01:56:55.483
Hello, Harry.

01:56:56.403 --> 01:57:01.573
-What do you want?
-To ask you how you died.

01:57:03.953 --> 01:57:06.413
lt was dreadful.

01:57:06.573 --> 01:57:10.243
lt happened right here
in this very cubicle.

01:57:10.413 --> 01:57:14.463
l'd hidden because Olive Hornby
was teasing me about my glasses.

01:57:14.623 --> 01:57:19.553
l was crying, and then
l heard somebody come in.

01:57:19.713 --> 01:57:26.053
-Who was it, Myrtle?
-l don't know. l was distraught!

01:57:27.343 --> 01:57:30.763
But they said something funny,
a kind of made-up language.

01:57:30.933 --> 01:57:37.273
And l realized it was a boy, so l unlocked
the door to tell him to go away and. . .

01:57:38.443 --> 01:57:43.283
-. . .l died.
-Just like that? How?

01:57:43.443 --> 01:57:47.953
l just remember seeing a pair
of great, big, yellow eyes. . .

01:57:48.123 --> 01:57:51.953
. . .over there by that sink.

01:58:17.063 --> 01:58:19.103
This is it.

01:58:19.983 --> 01:58:24.823
This is it, Ron. l think this is
the entrance to the Chamber of Secrets.

01:58:26.823 --> 01:58:31.663
Say something. Harry,
say something in Parseltongue.

01:59:23.213 --> 01:59:27.303
Excellent, Harry. Good work.
Well, then, l'll just be. . . .

01:59:27.463 --> 01:59:29.723
There's no need for me to stay.

01:59:30.343 --> 01:59:32.223
Yes, there is.

01:59:34.053 --> 01:59:37.143
-You first.
-Now, boys, what good will it do?

01:59:37.313 --> 01:59:38.643
Better you than us.

01:59:39.853 --> 01:59:42.773
But-- Obviously, yes.

01:59:47.073 --> 01:59:49.783
Sure you don't want to test it first?

01:59:56.583 --> 01:59:59.833
lt's really quite filthy down here.

02:00:00.293 --> 02:00:04.843
-All right. Let's go.
-Oh, Harry?

02:00:05.253 --> 02:00:10.173
lf you die down there,
you're welcome to share my toilet.

02:00:12.723 --> 02:00:14.683
Thanks, Myrtle.

02:00:43.793 --> 02:00:48.963
Now, remember: Any sign of movement,
close your eyes straightaway.

02:00:49.923 --> 02:00:51.593
Go on.

02:00:55.303 --> 02:00:56.643
This way.

02:01:03.643 --> 02:01:08.903
-What's this?
-lt looks like a snake.

02:01:09.073 --> 02:01:12.743
-lt's a snakeskin.
-Bloody hell.

02:01:12.903 --> 02:01:18.703
Whatever shed this must be
60 feet long. Or more.

02:01:20.623 --> 02:01:23.583
Heart of a lion, this one.

02:01:27.293 --> 02:01:31.963
The adventure ends here, boys.
But don't fret.

02:01:33.883 --> 02:01:39.353
The world will know our story.
How l was too late to save the girl.

02:01:39.683 --> 02:01:43.183
How you two
tragically lost your minds. . .

02:01:43.353 --> 02:01:46.353
. . .at the sight of her mangled body.

02:01:47.193 --> 02:01:48.653
So. . . .

02:01:49.773 --> 02:01:52.113
You first, Mr. Potter.

02:01:52.363 --> 02:01:55.533
Say goodbye to your memories.

02:01:57.573 --> 02:01:59.533
Obliviate!

02:02:33.443 --> 02:02:36.573
-Ron! Ron, are you okay?
-l'm fine.

02:02:40.323 --> 02:02:42.083
Hello.

02:02:42.743 --> 02:02:44.583
Who are you?

02:02:45.953 --> 02:02:48.623
-Ron Weasley.
-Really?

02:02:48.793 --> 02:02:51.673
And who am l?

02:02:53.423 --> 02:02:57.763
Lockhart's Memory Charm backfired.
He hasn't got a clue who he is.

02:02:58.093 --> 02:03:02.603
lt's an odd sort of place, isn't it?

02:03:02.763 --> 02:03:04.893
Do you live here?

02:03:05.603 --> 02:03:08.103
-No.
-Really?

02:03:12.693 --> 02:03:14.483
-What do l do now?
-You wait here. . .

02:03:14.653 --> 02:03:17.613
. . .and try and shift some of this rock
so we can get back through.

02:03:17.783 --> 02:03:21.453
-l'll go on and find Ginny.
-Okay.

02:04:54.673 --> 02:04:58.553
Ginny! Ginny, please don't be dead.
Wake up, wake up.

02:04:59.053 --> 02:05:01.133
Please wake up.

02:05:01.383 --> 02:05:03.553
She won't wake.

02:05:09.013 --> 02:05:13.353
Tom. Tom Riddle.
What do you mean, she won't wake?

02:05:13.523 --> 02:05:16.903
-She's not. . .?
-She's still alive, but only just.

02:05:17.903 --> 02:05:20.193
-Are you a ghost?
-A memory. . .

02:05:20.363 --> 02:05:22.743
. . .preserved in a diary for 50 years.

02:05:25.413 --> 02:05:30.623
She's cold as ice.
Ginny, please don't be dead. Wake up.

02:05:30.793 --> 02:05:33.213
You've got to help me, Tom.
There's a basilisk.

02:05:33.373 --> 02:05:35.963
lt won't come until it's called.

02:05:38.753 --> 02:05:41.593
-Give me my wand, Tom.
-You won't be needing it.

02:05:42.633 --> 02:05:46.053
-We've got to go. We've got to save her.
-l'm afraid l can't do that.

02:05:46.223 --> 02:05:50.263
You see, as poor Ginny grows weaker,
l grow stronger.

02:05:51.603 --> 02:05:56.103
Yes, Harry, it was Ginny Weasley
who opened the Chamber of Secrets.

02:05:56.273 --> 02:05:58.613
No. She couldn't. She wouldn't.

02:05:58.773 --> 02:06:01.983
lt was Ginny who set the basilisk
on the Mudbloods and Filch's cat. . .

02:06:02.153 --> 02:06:04.613
. . .Ginny who wrote the threatening
messages on the walls.

02:06:04.783 --> 02:06:08.073
-But why?
-Because l told her to.

02:06:08.243 --> 02:06:13.203
You'll find l can be very persuasive.
Not that she knew what she was doing.

02:06:13.373 --> 02:06:16.713
She was, shall we say,
in a kind of trance.

02:06:17.253 --> 02:06:19.753
Still, the power of the diary
began to scare her.

02:06:19.923 --> 02:06:22.303
She tried to dispose of it
in the girls' bathroom.

02:06:22.463 --> 02:06:26.803
And then who should find it but you?

02:06:26.973 --> 02:06:30.103
The very person
l was most anxious to meet.

02:06:30.683 --> 02:06:32.773
And why did you want to meet me?

02:06:33.143 --> 02:06:36.523
l knew l had to talk to you,
meet you if l could.

02:06:36.693 --> 02:06:39.983
So l decided to show you my capture
of that brainless oaf Hagrid. . .

02:06:40.153 --> 02:06:43.323
-. . .to gain your trust.
-Hagrid's my friend.

02:06:44.233 --> 02:06:48.823
-And you framed him, didn't you?
-lt was my word against Hagrid's.

02:06:48.993 --> 02:06:52.283
Only Dumbledore seemed to think
he was innocent.

02:06:52.453 --> 02:06:54.623
l'll bet Dumbledore saw
right through you.

02:06:54.793 --> 02:06:58.253
He certainly kept an annoyingly close
watch on me after that.

02:06:58.423 --> 02:07:01.713
l knew it wouldn't be safe to open the
Chamber again while l was at school. . .

02:07:01.883 --> 02:07:03.713
. . .so l decided to leave behind
a diary. . .

02:07:03.883 --> 02:07:06.013
. . .preserving my 1 6-year-old self
in its pages. . .

02:07:06.173 --> 02:07:08.843
. . .so that one day
l would be able to lead another. . .

02:07:09.013 --> 02:07:11.853
. . .to finish Salazar Slytherin's
noble work.

02:07:12.013 --> 02:07:14.263
Well, you haven't finished it
this time.

02:07:14.433 --> 02:07:17.393
ln a few hours, the Mandrake Draught
will be ready.

02:07:17.563 --> 02:07:20.313
And everyone who was Petrified
will be all right again.

02:07:20.693 --> 02:07:25.943
Haven't l told you? Killing Mudbloods
doesn't matter to me anymore.

02:07:26.193 --> 02:07:30.993
For many months now,
my new target has been you.

02:07:32.453 --> 02:07:36.043
How is it that a baby
with no extraordinary magical talent. . .

02:07:36.203 --> 02:07:38.873
. . .was able to defeat the greatest wizard
of all time?

02:07:39.213 --> 02:07:42.173
How did you escape with nothing
but a scar. . .

02:07:42.333 --> 02:07:44.713
. . .while Lord Voldemort's powers
were destroyed?

02:07:44.883 --> 02:07:49.053
Why do you care how l escaped?
Voldemort was after your time.

02:07:49.223 --> 02:07:55.723
Voldemort is my past,
present and future.

02:08:16.123 --> 02:08:19.583
You. You're the Heir of Slytherin.

02:08:22.753 --> 02:08:26.343
-You're Voldemort.
-Surely you didn't think. . .

02:08:26.503 --> 02:08:31.013
. . .l was going to keep
my filthy Muggle father's name?

02:08:31.183 --> 02:08:35.353
No. l fashioned myself a new name,
a name l knew wizards everywhere. . .

02:08:35.513 --> 02:08:39.733
. . .would fear to speak when l became
the greatest sorcerer in the world.

02:08:39.893 --> 02:08:43.063
Albus Dumbledore
is the greatest sorcerer in the world.

02:08:43.233 --> 02:08:46.613
Dumbledore's been driven out of
this castle by the mere memory of me.

02:08:46.823 --> 02:08:51.863
He'll never be gone. Not as long as
those who remain are loyal to him.

02:08:58.243 --> 02:08:59.293
Fawkes?

02:09:15.553 --> 02:09:19.143
So this is what Dumbledore
sends his great defender.

02:09:19.313 --> 02:09:22.983
A songbird and an old hat.

02:09:36.283 --> 02:09:40.833
Let's match the power of Lord
Voldemort, Heir of Salazar Slytherin. . .

02:09:41.003 --> 02:09:45.003
. . .against the famous Harry Potter.

02:09:58.353 --> 02:10:02.683
Parseltongue won't save you now,
Potter. lt only obeys me.

02:10:32.883 --> 02:10:34.423
No!

02:10:34.883 --> 02:10:39.393
Your bird may have blinded the basilisk,
but it can still hear you.

02:12:21.363 --> 02:12:24.663
Yes, Potter.
The process is nearly complete.

02:12:24.833 --> 02:12:29.753
ln a few minutes, Ginny Weasley will be
dead, and l will cease to be a memory.

02:12:29.913 --> 02:12:32.583
Lord Voldemort will return. . .

02:12:32.963 --> 02:12:37.173
. . .very much alive.

02:12:37.883 --> 02:12:39.303
Ginny?

02:14:55.643 --> 02:14:57.233
Remarkable, isn't it. . .

02:14:57.393 --> 02:15:01.403
. . .how quickly the venom
of the basilisk penetrates the body?

02:15:01.573 --> 02:15:04.233
l'd guess you have little more
than a minute to live.

02:15:04.573 --> 02:15:08.613
You'll be with your dear
Mudblood mother soon, Harry.

02:15:13.623 --> 02:15:17.293
Funny, the damage a silly
little book can do. . .

02:15:17.463 --> 02:15:22.503
. . .especially in the hands
of a silly little girl.

02:15:25.343 --> 02:15:27.173
What are you doing?

02:15:30.013 --> 02:15:32.143
Stop. No!

02:16:30.403 --> 02:16:34.413
lt was me.
But l swear, l didn't mean to.

02:16:34.583 --> 02:16:38.083
Riddle made me, and. . . .

02:16:38.583 --> 02:16:41.253
Harry, you're hurt.

02:16:41.583 --> 02:16:43.083
Don't worry.

02:16:43.253 --> 02:16:46.923
Ginny, you need
to get yourself out.

02:16:47.093 --> 02:16:50.343
Follow the Chamber
and you'll find Ron.

02:17:02.483 --> 02:17:04.613
You were brilliant, Fawkes.

02:17:05.733 --> 02:17:08.153
l just wasn't quick enough.

02:17:28.963 --> 02:17:30.673
Of course.

02:17:30.973 --> 02:17:33.803
Phoenix tears have healing powers.

02:17:35.433 --> 02:17:37.223
Thanks.

02:17:38.973 --> 02:17:41.103
lt's all right, Ginny.

02:17:42.233 --> 02:17:44.443
lt's over.

02:17:45.443 --> 02:17:47.983
lt's just a memory.

02:17:50.863 --> 02:17:56.203
Amazing!
This is just like magic!

02:18:07.503 --> 02:18:10.173
You both realize, of course. . .

02:18:10.343 --> 02:18:15.843
. . .that in the past few hours, you have
broken perhaps a dozen school rules.

02:18:16.473 --> 02:18:17.513
Yes, sir.

02:18:17.683 --> 02:18:20.893
There is sufficient evidence
to have you both expelled.

02:18:21.063 --> 02:18:22.273
Yes, sir.

02:18:22.433 --> 02:18:25.193
Therefore, it is only fitting. . .

02:18:26.733 --> 02:18:29.023
. . .that you both receive. . .

02:18:29.523 --> 02:18:33.613
. . .Special Awards for Services
to the School.

02:18:35.703 --> 02:18:37.533
Thanks, sir.

02:18:38.123 --> 02:18:40.413
Now, Mr. Weasley, if you would. . .

02:18:40.583 --> 02:18:44.753
. . .have an owl deliver these
release papers to Azkaban.

02:18:45.873 --> 02:18:50.633
l believe we want
our gamekeeper back.

02:18:55.593 --> 02:18:59.933
First, l want to thank you, Harry.

02:19:00.553 --> 02:19:04.063
You must have shown me
real loyalty down in the Chamber.

02:19:04.933 --> 02:19:09.523
Nothing but that
could have called Fawkes to you.

02:19:11.903 --> 02:19:13.443
And. . .

02:19:14.033 --> 02:19:15.443
. . .second. . .

02:19:15.613 --> 02:19:20.413
. . .l sense that something
is troubling you.

02:19:20.623 --> 02:19:23.123
Am l right, Harry?

02:19:24.953 --> 02:19:26.713
lt's just. . . .

02:19:27.873 --> 02:19:32.593
You see, sir, l couldn't help
but notice certain things, certain. . . .

02:19:32.753 --> 02:19:38.433
Certain similarities
between Tom Riddle and me.

02:19:38.973 --> 02:19:40.183
l see.

02:19:40.343 --> 02:19:46.143
Well, you can speak
Parseltongue, Harry. Why?

02:19:46.603 --> 02:19:52.113
Because Lord Voldemort
can speak Parseltongue.

02:19:53.323 --> 02:19:56.073
lf l'm not mistaken, Harry. . .

02:19:56.443 --> 02:20:00.283
. . .he transferred
some of his powers to you. . .

02:20:00.453 --> 02:20:03.413
. . .the night he gave you that scar.

02:20:03.583 --> 02:20:07.453
Voldemort transferred
some of his powers to me?

02:20:09.373 --> 02:20:12.083
Not intentionally. . .

02:20:12.963 --> 02:20:14.883
. . .but yes.

02:20:16.803 --> 02:20:20.133
So the Sorting Hat was right.
l should be in Slytherin.

02:20:20.303 --> 02:20:25.143
lt's true. You possess many of the
qualities that Voldemort himself prizes.

02:20:25.313 --> 02:20:28.143
Determination, resourcefulness. . .

02:20:28.313 --> 02:20:32.313
. . .and if l may say so,
a certain disregard for the rules.

02:20:33.023 --> 02:20:37.033
Why, then, did the Sorting Hat
place you in Gryffindor?

02:20:37.863 --> 02:20:41.533
-Because l asked it to.
-Exactly, Harry. Exactly.

02:20:41.703 --> 02:20:43.783
Which makes you different
from Voldemort.

02:20:43.953 --> 02:20:47.833
lt is not our abilities
that show what we truly are.

02:20:48.123 --> 02:20:50.253
lt is our choices.

02:20:53.923 --> 02:20:57.343
lf you want proof
why you belong in Gryffindor. . .

02:20:57.503 --> 02:21:02.383
. . .then l suggest
you look more closely at this.

02:21:03.393 --> 02:21:05.053
Be careful.

02:21:10.733 --> 02:21:13.403
Godric Gryffindor.

02:21:13.563 --> 02:21:17.653
lt would take a true Gryffindor
to pull that out of the hat.

02:21:26.533 --> 02:21:27.913
Dobby.

02:21:29.203 --> 02:21:33.583
So this is your master.
The family you serve is the Malfoys.

02:21:35.753 --> 02:21:39.093
l'll deal with you later.

02:21:44.933 --> 02:21:46.553
Out of my way, Potter.

02:21:46.723 --> 02:21:50.313
So it's true. You have returned.

02:21:50.983 --> 02:21:53.773
When the governors learned that
Arthur Weasley's daughter. . .

02:21:53.943 --> 02:21:58.113
. . .was taken into the Chamber,
they saw fit to summon me back.

02:21:58.943 --> 02:22:03.033
-Ridiculous.
-Curiously, Lucius, several of them. . .

02:22:03.203 --> 02:22:06.873
. . .were under the impression
that you would curse their family. . .

02:22:07.033 --> 02:22:09.873
. . .if they did not agree
to suspend me in the first place.

02:22:10.333 --> 02:22:13.793
-How dare you!
-Beg your pardon?

02:22:13.963 --> 02:22:17.753
My sole concern has always been
and will always be. . .

02:22:17.923 --> 02:22:20.753
. . .the welfare of this school. . .

02:22:20.923 --> 02:22:25.223
. . .and, of course, its students.

02:22:29.263 --> 02:22:33.483
The culprit has been identified,
l presume?

02:22:33.853 --> 02:22:35.393
Yes.

02:22:36.983 --> 02:22:38.813
And?

02:22:39.983 --> 02:22:42.033
Who was it?

02:22:48.453 --> 02:22:50.993
Voldemort.

02:22:52.163 --> 02:22:57.623
Only this time he chose to act
through somebody else. . .

02:22:58.173 --> 02:23:01.803
. . .by means of this.

02:23:04.473 --> 02:23:06.013
l see.

02:23:07.473 --> 02:23:11.683
Fortunately, our young Mr. Potter
discovered it.

02:23:12.013 --> 02:23:15.683
One hopes that no more of Lord
Voldemort's old school-things. . .

02:23:15.853 --> 02:23:19.103
. . .should find their way
into innocent hands.

02:23:19.443 --> 02:23:23.363
The consequences for the one
responsible would be. . .

02:23:23.733 --> 02:23:25.613
. . .severe.

02:23:27.033 --> 02:23:29.823
Well, let us hope. . .

02:23:29.993 --> 02:23:35.543
. . .that Mr. Potter will always
be around to save the day.

02:23:36.293 --> 02:23:40.043
Don't worry. l will be.

02:23:48.803 --> 02:23:50.843
Dumbledore.

02:23:51.973 --> 02:23:55.523
Come, Dobby. We're leaving.

02:24:12.783 --> 02:24:17.253
Sir?
l wonder if l could have that?

02:24:23.673 --> 02:24:25.253
Mr. Malfoy.

02:24:25.423 --> 02:24:27.633
Mr. Malfoy!

02:24:28.093 --> 02:24:30.263
l have something of yours.

02:24:31.933 --> 02:24:34.893
Mine? l don't know
what you're talking about.

02:24:35.063 --> 02:24:36.603
l think you do, sir.

02:24:36.773 --> 02:24:39.893
l think you slipped the diary
into Ginny Weasley's cauldron. . .

02:24:40.063 --> 02:24:41.483
. . .that day at Diagon Alley.

02:24:42.193 --> 02:24:44.733
You do, do you?

02:24:52.073 --> 02:24:55.163
Why don't you prove it?

02:25:01.423 --> 02:25:03.583
Come, Dobby.

02:25:04.883 --> 02:25:06.923
Open it.

02:25:10.423 --> 02:25:11.973
Dobby.

02:25:12.133 --> 02:25:15.303
Master has given Dobby a sock.

02:25:15.603 --> 02:25:17.683
What? l didn't give--

02:25:17.853 --> 02:25:21.563
Master has presented Dobby
with clothes.

02:25:21.733 --> 02:25:24.773
Dobby is free.

02:25:31.323 --> 02:25:35.073
You lost me my servant!

02:25:42.043 --> 02:25:46.043
You shall not harm Harry Potter.

02:25:58.183 --> 02:26:01.893
Your parents were
meddlesome fools too.

02:26:02.063 --> 02:26:05.233
Mark my words, Potter.
One day soon. . .

02:26:05.403 --> 02:26:10.613
. . .you are going to meet
the same sticky end.

02:26:16.323 --> 02:26:22.203
Harry Potter freed Dobby.
How can Dobby ever repay him?

02:26:22.583 --> 02:26:26.833
-Just promise me something.
-Anything, sir.

02:26:28.793 --> 02:26:31.263
Never try to save my life again.

02:26:37.393 --> 02:26:40.393
-Welcome back, Sir Nicholas.
-Thank you.

02:26:40.683 --> 02:26:43.063
-Good evening, Sir Nicholas.
-Good evening.

02:26:43.233 --> 02:26:46.153
-Good to see you, Sir Nicholas.
-Thank you.

02:26:47.523 --> 02:26:49.733
Hello.

02:26:51.443 --> 02:26:56.073
-Hermione! Welcome back.
-Thanks, Sir Nicholas.

02:26:59.333 --> 02:27:02.663
Harry. lt's Hermione.

02:27:29.483 --> 02:27:33.193
-Welcome back, Hermione.
-lt's good to be back.

02:27:33.363 --> 02:27:35.943
Congratulations.
l can't believe you solved it.

02:27:36.113 --> 02:27:38.363
We had loads of help from you.

02:27:38.533 --> 02:27:41.743
-We couldn't have done it without you.
-Thanks.

02:27:43.583 --> 02:27:46.543
Could l have your attention, please?

02:27:50.713 --> 02:27:53.213
Before we begin the feast. . .

02:27:53.383 --> 02:27:59.643
. . .let us have a round of applause
for Professor Sprout, Madam Pomfrey. . .

02:27:59.803 --> 02:28:03.933
. . .whose Mandrake juice has been
so successfully administered. . .

02:28:04.103 --> 02:28:06.773
. . .to all who had been Petrified.

02:28:17.283 --> 02:28:20.283
Also, in light of the recent events. . .

02:28:20.453 --> 02:28:22.623
. . .as a school treat. . .

02:28:22.783 --> 02:28:26.753
. . .all exams have been canceled.

02:28:29.423 --> 02:28:31.003
Oh, no.

02:28:47.933 --> 02:28:49.983
Sorry l'm late.

02:28:56.033 --> 02:29:00.453
The owl that delivered my release papers
got all lost and confused.

02:29:00.783 --> 02:29:04.073
Some ruddy bird called Errol.

02:29:19.843 --> 02:29:25.853
And l'd just like to say that if it hadn't
been for you, Harry and Ron. . .

02:29:26.063 --> 02:29:29.023
. . .and Hermione, of course. . .

02:29:29.683 --> 02:29:33.773
. . .l would still be you-know-where. . .

02:29:33.943 --> 02:29:37.523
. . .so l'd just like to say thanks.

02:29:46.913 --> 02:29:49.873
There's no Hogwarts
without you, Hagrid.
